{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars","id":910996,"title":"3rd Edition Lookshy and Solars.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T11:49:49-07:00","id":910996,"title":"3rd Edition Lookshy and Solars.","content":"So I thought that it was worth asking how Lookshy would react to a Solar in 3rd edition? Previous editions portrayed Lookshy as deeply pragmatic and that while they disliked Anathema they seemed to be willing to work with them for mutual benefit.<br /> <br /> 3rd Edition has explicitly shown a fanatical and much more importantly Immaculate Lookshy, does this mean that Lookshy is now at a stage that they unwilling to work with Anathema regardless of interest?<br /> <br /> At the same time the changes to crafting and the introduction of Workings makes something Craft or Occult Supernal Twilight absurdly valuable, to say nothing about the value of a War-Supernal Dawn that could literally make Gunzosha quality troops the mainstay of your forces. Just thought that it would be interesting to speculate until more concrete information is available.<br /> <br /> To be clear I am referring to the leadership since common people wanting to lynch Celestials being the global norm is far from new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:59:38-07:00","id":911007,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading though the new book (649 pages? Sheesh!) but i'd probably say that the individual commanders will be pragmatic as they need to be, some will be fanatical to the degree of Idiocy/self-destruction others will be extremely pragmatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:01:16-07:00","id":911009,"title":"","content":"I don't know what will be canon, but I'd portray Lookshy with a some good old fashion pragmatic hypocrisy. On one hand, they hunt down Anathema with as much vigor as the Realm. On the other hand, they have some poor Twilight locked up in a top secret manse, producing new artifacts. It's only a matter of time before this Twilight realizes that they are being used and figures out &quot;Hey, maybe instead of taking orders,<b> I </b>could be running things.&quot; At which point, the General Staff will off the Anathema and wait for the next inevitable Twilight Exaltation*.<br /> <br /> *Come on! Lookshian Twilight has to be one of the most common character types in Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:08:14-07:00","id":911019,"title":"","content":"Lookshy is run by military pragmatists, but they're also an Immaculate town, even if it's their own state church rather than the same Immaculate Order that is embedded in the Realm. They maintain their own equivalent of the Wyld Hunt, and would never be seen using Solars openly. <br /> <br /> That said, it's not out of the realm of possibility that the leadership may use Solars covertly. Night Caste are particularly valuable in this sense, because they excel at remaining covert. Twilight as well, because a single Twilight can serve as an incredibly effective military support... but more forward and public Castes are something they'd probably not be willing to fold into existing forces. More likely, they'd act through intermediaries to contract such heroes into situations that they need a wrench thrown into. Having a Dawn train or lead standing Lookshy forces? The troops wouldn't stand for it. Have the Spec Ops Night Caste whose status as a Solar Anathema is classified join a Circle of Solars in order to steer them into situations that Lookshy would like resolved? Absolutely. <br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that the leadership inevitably won't like them... But if it can be done out of the light of day, and could keep Lookshy soldiers from going into battle, they might be willing to use them. It's chess (or Gateway if you prefer), the Solar is an expendable piece that can be used to great effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11867,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","user":"Caffeine Delusions","date":". 06-10-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:12:00-07:00","id":911022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911019#post911019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Have the Spec Ops Night Caste whose status as a Solar Anathema is classified join a Circle of Solars in order to steer them into situations that Lookshy would like resolved? Absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to play this character now.<br /> <br /> /adds to the pile of Lookshy based character concepts.<br /> <br /> ((Also add a Lookshian Dawn that gets run out of town by the Wyld Hunt, who finds out about the Lookshian Night Caste who was given rank in Military Intelligence. Epic Rivalry Ensures. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 06-09-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:13:02-07:00","id":911024,"title":"","content":"Lookshy may be a different branch of the Immaculate tree (the original trunk, really), but they're still Immaculates, and they still have a Purist faction that doesn't just not like Solars, Lunars, and Abyssals, it also doesn't like one of its allies (Great Forks) for being openly ruled by gods and having so many God-Blooded, as well as being a Mecca for Exigents (that last one being a recent feature from EX3). While the faction is not the majority by any means, Karal Linwei is in a potentially career-ending crisis, not a mild upset, over her daughter being a Zenith, and Fire Orchid's story makes no sense if Solars can work so directly with the Seventh. Really, the only difference is that what they do is actually called a Wyld Hunt now.<br /> <br /> As for the utility of the Solars, it's arguably less in this edition, on account of Dragon-Blooded being able to make Artifact 4 - N/A stuff with ratings of 5 in an Ability, and being able to get anything short of an Ambition 3 Solar working by dint of hard work. They'd probably rather continue working on their own than be beholden to a weak link that needs protection and may also, in fact, be a demon in a flesh suit, which reflects poorly on both metic Solars and natives of Lookshy that become Celestials, since the former can't be trusted and the latter are suspect because only the spiritually weak and vulnerable who take excessive risks and potentially disrupt unit cohesion become Anathema, and everyone &quot;knows&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:49:57-07:00","id":911056,"title":"","content":"Wyld Hunts issue from Lookshy, even if they're not specifically funded by the government the way that they are in the Realm; they're a private interest.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd say that if Mnemon, of all people, can be plausibly written as making a brief pact with the Mask of Winters via an Abyssal Exalt intermediary, then somebody with authority in Lookshy might do so on a case by case basis, even if that person still thinks the one they're dealing with is an abomination and they'll be looking to help out with destroying them at the earliest possible opportunity.<br /> <br /> It's a lot like how Hitler really hated Communism, but was still able to manage to reach an agreement with the Soviet Union that held up for a few years, until he went with the whole &quot;time to destroy Communism&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Or how Churchill and Roosevelt really hated Communism, and were still able to form an alliance to conduct a war and divvy up occupation of Germany that held up for a few years, until they went with the whole &quot;let's don nothing to really alleviate or compromise with your legitimate fears of future western invasion, so it all comes to a head more explosively&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> So it may be that forming alliances with Anathema that you know you will inevitably have to destroy is not the best course of action. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:28:31-07:00","id":911100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911022#post911022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to play this character now.<br /> <br /> /adds to the pile of Lookshy based character concepts.<br /> <br /> ((Also add a Lookshian Dawn that gets run out of town by the Wyld Hunt, who finds out about the Lookshian Night Caste who was given rank in Military Intelligence. Epic Rivalry Ensures. ))</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Glad to serve. It's actually the concept behind a stock character of mine; Adamant Viper. Yes, his name is a blatant send-up of Solid Snake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:47:35-07:00","id":911116,"title":"","content":"I'm... Still toying with the Idea of a Lookshyian Gunzhosha(?) Armour wearer who Exalted as a Dawn caste while in combat.. He's managed to get away with staying in the military by staying in the armour and keeping the Charm use to a minimum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:50:41-07:00","id":911119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911116#post911116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm... Still toying with the Idea of a Lookshyian Gunzhosha(?) Armour wearer who Exalted as a Dawn caste while in combat.. He's managed to get away with staying in the military by staying in the armour and keeping the Charm use to a minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your Dawn could be buddies with my Chosen of Ending Gunzhosha Commando.... if your Dawn can remember who he is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:19:39-07:00","id":911137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911022#post911022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to play this character now.<br /> <br /> /adds to the pile of Lookshy based character concepts.<br /> <br /> ((Also add a Lookshian Dawn that gets run out of town by the Wyld Hunt, who finds out about the Lookshian Night Caste who was given rank in Military Intelligence. Epic Rivalry Ensures. ))</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have played that character (More or less)<br /> <br /> My character was a Shinobi for Gens Karal (SP?) who, while on a mission, Exalted as a Night Caste. Hating what he now was, and being a staunchly loyal citizen, he continued to do his duty, just taking further and further ranging tasks, meticulously making sure that what he was stayed hidden.<br /> <br /> My Circle eventually figured out he wasn't just some peasant, and he was outted as a Night Caste (By Five Days Darkness, since I was apparently the reincarnation of Ebon Shadow's Daughter), but when the game came to a shitty sudden end, the Circle had still never found out his true purpose, and that he was actively spying on/working against them.<br /> <br /> Hell of a lot of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:24:28-07:00","id":911191,"title":"","content":"A decent chunk of the &quot;pragmatic with regards to Anathema&quot; image of Lookshy was confusion on the part of the writers who had those sections (per Neph, long, long ago). Lookshy is pragmatic, but it's also full-bore Immaculate. It's worth remembering the power of Celestials threatens Dragon-Blooded hegemony. It's also worth remembering that Lunars want to destroy Lookshy as much as they want to destroy the Realm, so Lookshyan soldiers get the pleasure of fighting asymmetric campaigns against Lunar-led armies. Both are squatting on the legacy of the First Age, which the Lunars feel belongs to them. Even non-religious Lookshyans believe Lunars and Solars are Anathema. To them, that's just factual. Expecting them to casually deal or recruit world-endangering Demons because they don't show up to church is kinda silly.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean deals won't occur, of course. It just means those deals are closer to those movies where the CIA cuts deals with the Mafia or drug lords. Nobody trusts anybody, there are lots of readied weapons at all times, and chances are both sides have plans to eliminate or expose the other as soon as it's tenable.<br /> <br /> If I were a member of the General Staff of Lookshy, the idea of steering a full Circle of Solars to do my bidding would be roughly as appealing as saddle-breaking a Behemoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:44:14-07:00","id":911200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911024#post911024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the utility of the Solars, it's arguably less in this edition, on account of Dragon-Blooded being able to make Artifact 4 - N/A stuff with ratings of 5 in an Ability, and being able to get anything short of an Ambition 3 Solar working by dint of hard work.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they getting the thirty-some-odd successes each Craft interval?<br /> <br /> Likewise, I wouldn't imply that achieving a Solar Working of <i>any</i> Ambition is something DBs would look on as reliable. To put it shortly, even going with Finesse 1 and a fistful of Means, the dice math is really against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-09-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:59:15-07:00","id":911209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911191#post911191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A decent chunk of the &quot;pragmatic with regards to Anathema&quot; image of Lookshy was confusion on the part of the writers who had those sections (per Neph, long, long ago). Lookshy is pragmatic, but it's also full-bore Immaculate. It's worth remembering the power of Celestials threatens Dragon-Blooded hegemony. It's also worth remembering that Lunars want to destroy Lookshy as much as they want to destroy the Realm, so Lookshyan soldiers get the pleasure of fighting asymmetric campaigns against Lunar-led armies. Both are squatting on the legacy of the First Age, which the Lunars feel belongs to them. Even non-religious Lookshyans believe Lunars and Solars are Anathema. To them, that's just factual. Expecting them to casually deal or recruit world-endangering Demons because they don't show up to church is kinda silly.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean deals won't occur, of course. It just means those deals are closer to those movies where the CIA cuts deals with the Mafia or drug lords. Nobody trusts anybody, there are lots of readied weapons at all times, and chances are both sides have plans to eliminate or expose the other as soon as it's tenable.<br /> <br /> If I were a member of the General Staff of Lookshy, the idea of steering a full Circle of Solars to do my bidding would be roughly as appealing as saddle-breaking a Behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is quickly becoming a reservation of mine when dealing with 3rd (even though it has done a marvelous job of convincing me until now), I feel like it makes Lookshy and the Realm too similar, I always thought that Lookshy had a very Shinto approach to their faith with it being very secondary to their ancient Greek style Nationalism. It really does just feel painfully unnecessary to have yet another group devouted to ending Solars. It should honestly at least occur to at least some Lookshyians that a Solar could be Lookshyian first and Anathema second.<br /> <br /> A vibe that I loved from 1st edition was that people viewed Solars and Lunars as extremely different things, both were Anathema but while Lunars were active threats that are a well known quantity. Solars on the other hand were this mysterious force that were only well known by devout Immaculate historians (read:Sidereals) that no one really knew how to deal with other than that they were Anathema in extremely old legends. Nowadays everyone is suspiciously well-informed as to what they are and have very concrete opinions about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:59:15-07:00","id":911210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911191#post911191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A decent chunk of the &quot;pragmatic with regards to Anathema&quot; image of Lookshy was confusion on the part of the writers who had those sections (per Neph, long, long ago). Lookshy is pragmatic, but it's also full-bore Immaculate. It's worth remembering the power of Celestials threatens Dragon-Blooded hegemony. It's also worth remembering that Lunars want to destroy Lookshy as much as they want to destroy the Realm, so Lookshyan soldiers get the pleasure of fighting asymmetric campaigns against Lunar-led armies. Both are squatting on the legacy of the First Age, which the Lunars feel belongs to them. Even non-religious Lookshyans believe Lunars and Solars are Anathema. To them, that's just factual. Expecting them to casually deal or recruit world-endangering Demons because they don't show up to church is kinda silly.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean deals won't occur, of course. It just means those deals are closer to those movies where the CIA cuts deals with the Mafia or drug lords. Nobody trusts anybody, there are lots of readied weapons at all times, and chances are both sides have plans to eliminate or expose the other as soon as it's tenable.<br /> <br /> If I were a member of the General Staff of Lookshy, the idea of steering a full Circle of Solars to do my bidding would be roughly as appealing as saddle-breaking a Behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is quickly becoming a reservation of mine when dealing with 3rd (even though it has done a marvelous job of convincing me until now), I feel like it makes Lookshy and the Realm too similar, I always thought that Lookshy had a very Shinto approach to their faith with it being very secondary to their ancient Greek style Nationalism. It really does just feel painfully unnecessary to have yet another group devouted to ending Solars. It should honestly at least occur to at least some Lookshyians that a Solar could be Lookshyian first and Anathema second.<br /> <br /> A vibe that I loved from 1st edition was that people viewed Solars and Lunars as extremely different things, both were Anathema but while Lunars were active threats that are a well known quantity. Solars on the other hand were this mysterious force that were only well known by devout Immaculate historians (read:Sidereals) that no one really knew how to deal with other than that they were Anathema in extremely old legends. Nowadays everyone is suspiciously well-informed as to what they are and have very concrete opinions about them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Can anyone tell me how the same post got copied?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:18:38-07:00","id":911225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911200#post911200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are they getting the thirty-some-odd successes each Craft interval?<br /> <br /> Likewise, I wouldn't imply that achieving a Solar Working of <i>any</i> Ambition is something DBs would look on as reliable. To put it shortly, even going with Finesse 1 and a fistful of Means, the dice math is really against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can actually discuss that when the Dragon-Blooded book comes out and mechanically details them in this system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:23:57-07:00","id":911227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911210#post911210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Can anyone tell me how the same post got copied?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forum Ate it and Regurgitatied it? That or the Connection to the Forum was odd for abit and it read the Post message click twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:27:30-07:00","id":911229,"title":"","content":"Even back in earliest 1e, in <i>Castebook: Zenith</i>, the Lookshy General Staff were getting ready to hunt down and kill their own decorated, honored veteran, and daughter of one of their own membership, Karal Fire Orchid, for Exalting as a Solar. You'd think that if they had ever had enough pragmatism to work with a Solar, &quot;The one who's a loyal Lookshyan soldier and the daughter of one of our general staff, who Exalted protecting a village from a Fair Folk raid&quot; would be the one they'd be like &quot;Sure, she doesn't sound so bad&quot; about.<br /> <br /> But no. Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:30:58-07:00","id":911234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911225#post911225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can actually discuss that when the Dragon-Blooded book comes out and mechanically details them in this system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the &quot;extent&quot; to which <i>Solar</i> Charms can make a sorcerous working easier\u2026 I think we can discuss it now. I doubt DBs will be getting Charms that make them better at workings than Solars, let alone ones that enable Solar circle workings to be reliably accomplished with &quot;hard work.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:33:57-07:00","id":911236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911209#post911209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is quickly becoming a reservation of mine when dealing with 3rd (even though it has done a marvelous job of convincing me until now), I feel like it makes Lookshy and the Realm too similar, I always thought that Lookshy had a very Shinto approach to their faith with it being very secondary to their ancient Greek style Nationalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the matter of how different cultures can be sufficiently different even when they're practicing the same religion, I think the religions of the Realm and Lookshy can come across as sufficiently different when they're focused on details other than the Anathema. I mean, that they don't evangelize their religion or have it established makes for some pretty enormous differences in action and relationships.<br /> <br /> \u200bHaving similar reactions to outsiders doesn't erase those differences. I mean, look at how conflicting denominations of Christianity have generally related to things like Islam.<br /> <br /> And that's a matter of religious differences, not &quot;these are extremely dangerous and blasphemous entities who threaten the Dragon-sanctified reign of the Dragon Blooded over the Earth&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really does just feel painfully unnecessary to have yet another group devouted to ending Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's about consistency in the world Solars are returning to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It should honestly at least occur to at least some Lookshyians that a Solar could be Lookshyian first and Anathema second.</div> </div> </div> </div> It probably can. That then becomes a source of conflict, both internal and external.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:34:44-07:00","id":911237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911229#post911229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even back in earliest 1e, in <i>Castebook: Zenith</i>, the Lookshy General Staff were getting ready to hunt down and kill their own decorated, honored veteran, and daughter of one of their own membership, Karal Fire Orchid, for Exalting as a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but that is still not quite as bad as having your own Wyld Hunt which is made perfect sense for the Immaculate-heavy Realm but it feels unnecessary to make inquisition-style deathsquads an unnecessarily big part of the other major DB power since breaks down the contrast between the two more than is really needed, much less when considering that it comes across as any variant of the Immaculate being prone to zealotry.<br /> Also it is a big stretch to say that the General Staff was fully aware of her since her mother was acting on rumours and she wouldn't have been able to take any action no matter how covert if it became general knowledge among the General Staff (no pun intended) that they had anything concrete evidence to work with. And even that does not imply that they were near the 'go kill her' plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:37:41-07:00","id":911240,"title":"","content":"Lookshy does not have a Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople who come from Lookshy occasionally form Wyld Hunts.<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunt is what adherents of the Immaculate religion call a group of Dragon Blooded who get together to destroy Anathema; the idea of Immaculate Dragon Blooded who plan to go destroy a Solar not being a Wyld Hunt is a contradiction in terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:42:16-07:00","id":911247,"title":"","content":"(The confusion here stems from the Realm actually having a formalized organization they refer to as &quot;The Wyld Hunt,&quot; as examined in <i>Cult of the Illuminated,</i> who engage in Wyld Hunts, in addition to Wyld Hunts <i>in general </i>being whenever a group of Dragon-Blooded get together to crack down on some Anathema.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:43:07-07:00","id":911248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911240#post911240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lookshy does not have a Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> \u200bPeople who come from Lookshy occasionally form Wyld Hunts.<br /> <br /> Wyld Hunt is what adherents of the Immaculate religion call a group of Dragon Blooded who get together to destroy Anathema; the idea of Immaculate Dragon Blooded who plan to go destroy a Solar not being a Wyld Hunt is a contradiction in terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I am wrong but the Wyld Hunt has traditionally been a direct wing of the Realm Immaculate faith with their own resources and personnel, it it true that the bulk of the DBs are volunteers attending to it but they have most definitely been traditionally described as being led by a dedicated hunter-monk.<br /> <br /> Although maybe this can be chalked up to the phrase having an inconsistent meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:45:43-07:00","id":911252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911248#post911248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I am wrong but the Wyld Hunt has traditionally been a direct wing of the Realm Immaculate faith with their own resources and personnel, it it true that the bulk of the DBs are volunteers attending to it but they have most definitely been traditionally described as being led by a dedicated hunter-monk.<br /> <br /> Although maybe this can be chalked up to the phrase having an inconsistent meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inconsistent phrasing. In the Realm, the Wyld Hunt is a formal organization, but &quot;Wyld Hunt&quot; is <i>also</i> an <i>activity</i> which can be partaken of by any group of Dragon-Blooded. Ex3 emphasizes the latter, while Ex1 and 2 emphasized the former.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a group of Dragon-Blooded in the hinterlands and an Anathema comes calling, and you send for a Wyld Hunt and get told none is coming, then &quot;the Wyld Hunt&quot; is <i>you, </i>whether you feel up to it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:46:45-07:00","id":911253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911247#post911247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(The confusion here stems from the Realm actually having a formalized organization they refer to as &quot;The Wyld Hunt,&quot; as examined in <i>Cult of the Illuminated,</i> who engage in Wyld Hunts, in addition to Wyld Hunts <i>in general </i>being whenever a group of Dragon-Blooded get together to crack down on some Anathema.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this clarifies it quite a bit, groups that get just get together to hunt rather than a formalized organization is far more palatable than the institutionalized death-squads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:54:45-07:00","id":911262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911234#post911234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the &quot;extent&quot; to which <i>Solar</i> Charms can make a sorcerous working easier\u2026 I think we can discuss it now. I doubt DBs will be getting Charms that make them better at workings than Solars, let alone ones that enable Solar circle workings to be reliably accomplished with &quot;hard work.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Valkhawsen might have some strange shaping rituals or other miscellaneous powers in that regard. Things Solars wouldn't really practice, because there aren't that many of them and their workings and the like would probably tend to be a lot more individualistic. But Dragon-Blooded, all involved in the trade of a sorcerer-engineer, doing wai-tan junai things? They might be able to manage more productive teamwork. At minimum, we know that wide-scale teamwork for the Sorcerer Assistants can get two additional rolls on a working, if large numbers of them are working on a project.<br /> <br /> I mean, even if they get some weird Charms, they're still not going to be able to keep things up and running forever. They can't reverse the decay of the age, but they can do impressive things keeping some stuff around. At minimum, they have to be able to have kept all of the dwindling supplies they do have.<br /> <br /> Still, the Seventh Legion isn't going to stand for relying on potentially boobytrapped works of the Anathema. Not when they can still makes daiklaves and armor that are perfectly serviceable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:59:34-07:00","id":911265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911209#post911209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really does just feel painfully unnecessary to have yet another group devouted to ending Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire rest of the setting is pro-Solars. Only the two Immaculate places in the map hunt Solars. It's only those two places. In the /entire world/.<br /> <br /> Having only the Realm do it makes it seem like it is not part of the Immaculate credo, but rather the Realm being a bunch of meanies, which is not ideal.<br /> <br /> Having Lookshy be pro-Solar kind of railroads the Solars in the Scavenger Lands - a prime Solar playground - into Agents of Lookshy, which is also not ideal.<br /> <br /> It ALSO keeps this image of Lookshy as the 'pragmatic modern military good guys', which is just... terrible. Lookshy is a place, with an actual culture, that should impact its decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:59:38-07:00","id":911266,"title":"","content":"Pretty much. The simplest way I can put it is that Lookshy's 'Immaculate Chaplaincy' maintains a very small office responsible for organizing Wyld Hunts out of Lookshy's military, under the auspices and with the permissions of the Lookshy General Staff. It doesn't have near the reach or power of Wyld Hunts sponsored by the larger Immaculate Order and its dedicated 'Wyld Hunt' organization, as those can draw on the resources of the Realm, but it does exist, and it has seen use in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:31:35-07:00","id":911291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911265#post911265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The entire rest of the setting is pro-Solars. Only the two Immaculate places in the map hunt Solars. It's only those two places. In the /entire world/.<br /> <br /> Having only the Realm do it makes it seem like it is not part of the Immaculate credo, but rather the Realm being a bunch of meanies, which is not ideal.<br /> <br /> Having Lookshy be pro-Solar kind of railroads the Solars in the Scavenger Lands - a prime Solar playground - into Agents of Lookshy, which is also not ideal.<br /> <br /> It ALSO keeps this image of Lookshy as the 'pragmatic modern military good guys', which is just... terrible. Lookshy is a place, with an actual culture, that should impact its decisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>...It is worth noting that the rest of the world disdains Solars, there is no state that is pro-solar, there are just states willing to exploit them or tolerate them. Also underestimating the reach and power of the Realm is silly since virtually every location entry for a state mentions how the Realm controls it or how interesting it is that it is NOT a subject of the Realm. The only thing that lets the Solars breath is the Wyld being hampered severely by the brewing civil war and the Gold Faction otherwise it has traditionally been incredibly efficient at hunting exalts.Even Lunar domains are not safe since Lunar warlords are just as likely to kill you as they are if you misstep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:04:11-07:00","id":911313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911291#post911291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It is worth noting that the rest of the world disdains Solars, there is no state that is pro-solar, there are just states willing to exploit them or tolerate them. Also underestimating the reach and power of the Realm is silly since virtually every location entry for a state mentions how the Realm controls it or how interesting it is that it is NOT a subject of the Realm. The only thing that lets the Solars breath is the Wyld being hampered severely by the brewing civil war and the Gold Faction otherwise it has traditionally been incredibly efficient at hunting exalts.Even Lunar domains are not safe since Lunar warlords are just as likely to kill you as they are if you misstep.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is to say that 'They are pragmatic about Solars but can work with them' applies to the entirety of the setting aside from the Realm and Lookshy. Making saying 'do we really need another place that is anti-Solars' ring very, very weird. From the the Perfect of Paragon to the Haslanti League to the Onyx Archipelago and to Halta, all those will tolerate and ally with Solars out of pragmatism. Sample NPCs from 1e all work on those various locations.<br /> <br /> Places that are 'pragmatic about Solars, but will work with them' are dime a dozen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:13:19-07:00","id":911319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911313#post911313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is to say that 'They are pragmatic about Solars but can work with them' applies to the entirety of the setting aside from the Realm and Lookshy. Making saying 'do we really need another place that is anti-Solars' ring very, very weird. From the the Perfect of Paragon to the Haslanti League to the Onyx Archipelago and to Halta, all those will tolerate and ally with Solars out of pragmatism. Sample NPCs from 1e all work on those various locations.<br /> <br /> Places that are 'pragmatic about Solars, but will work with them' are dime a dozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>First it should be noted that not all of those places are really anywhere near 'friendly' and would turn on their deal almost immediately turn only *cough*Onyx*cough* and more importantly Lookshy is the only other major DB power, allowing for a story where Solars dont have to be forced to automatically work against any form of DB government out of a need for survival. Also I would point out that loyalty isnt really optional or even up for discussion when your sworn to the Perfect or dealing with Lunar elders.<br /> But your YMMV on that end since it depends on your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:25:36-07:00","id":911325,"title":"","content":"In past games I've had dynast NPCs who weren't above making deals with fair folk, demons or the &quot;demonic&quot; Anathema to further their own goals. In every society there are those for whom there is no low too low for them to stoop and would be even willing to deal with whatever they consider anathema to get what they want. In the decadent Realm such individuals weren't even that rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:34:26-07:00","id":911331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911056#post911056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'd say that if Mnemon, of all people, can be plausibly written as making a brief pact with the Mask of Winters via an Abyssal Exalt intermediary</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'll be surprised if that particular story element carries over to 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:50:47-07:00","id":911348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911319#post911319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First it should be noted that not all of those places are really anywhere near 'friendly' and would turn on their deal almost immediately turn only *cough*Onyx*cough*</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant pro-Solar in the same sense that Lookshy was described by you; again, as places that will ally with Solars in pragmatic ways.<br /> <br /> And Moray Darktide seems to be doing pretty well for himself working for Onyx and amassing his harem of pirate heroines, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:53:41-07:00","id":911352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911348#post911348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant pro-Solar in the same sense that Lookshy was described by you; again, as places that will ally with Solars in pragmatic ways.<br /> <br /> And Moray Darktide seems to be doing pretty well for himself working for Onyx and amassing his harem of pirate heroines, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point on the Harem, but he is usually shown to be blindingly loyal, not an ally which factors in heavily and even then the Prince seems to be considering offing him if he shows the slightest hesitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:55:49-07:00","id":911354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911331#post911331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'll be surprised if that particular story element carries over to 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about the event, it's about the concept. That's why I included the word &quot;plausibly&quot;; none of these things exist, what matters is if we can believe in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:06:29-07:00","id":911363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911352#post911352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point on the Harem, but he is usually shown to be blindingly loyal, not an ally which factors in heavily and even then the Prince seems to be considering offing him if he shows the slightest hesitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not because he's a Solar. That's just about the loyalty of powerful people generally. The Silver Prince doesn't seem to have any non-Solar allies either.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway. I think Lookshy should view Solars the way western countries view Islamic extremists. Sure, we dislike them, but it's not like we'd never help/fund them to fight someone else we hate. But we wouldn't admit it. As a military government, I expect that working with Solars is something they'd never admit or sanction, but there are off-the-books black-ops teams and research divisions who do whatever it takes, even work with Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:10:22-07:00","id":911364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911348#post911348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant pro-Solar in the same sense that Lookshy was described by you; again, as places that will ally with Solars in pragmatic ways.<br /> <br /> And Moray Darktide seems to be doing pretty well for himself working for Onyx and amassing his harem of pirate heroines, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also now that you pointed out the harem I am profoundly disturbed/amused since I went back to the castebooks and it really does seem like he should be presence-supernal since he is literally attracting celestial exalts like flies... Is Darktide intentionally meant to be the protagonist of a pirate-based harem anime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:14:08-07:00","id":911369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911363#post911363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway. I think Lookshy should view Solars the way western countries view Islamic extremists. Sure, we dislike them, but it's not like we'd never help/fund them to fight someone else we hate. But we wouldn't admit it. As a military government, I expect that working with Solars is something they'd never admit or sanction, but there are off-the-books black-ops teams and research divisions who do whatever it takes, even work with Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tricky thing there is that aside from a small handful, Solars have not been an overly prominent part of the setting in better than a thousand years. They've generally been hammered down almost as soon as they incarnate. It's explicitly because that restraint system is breaking down due to the impending dynastic struggle just as it's being made to deal with an unprecedented workload ten times larger than they'd previously been confronted with that the Solar Resurgence has been able to get its feet under it as a phenomenon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:18:18-07:00","id":911371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911352#post911352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point on the Harem, but he is usually shown to be blindingly loyal, not an ally which factors in heavily and even then the Prince seems to be considering offing him if he shows the slightest hesitation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Moray Darktide but I have never understood this. Why in Creation would the Prince not throw Darktide in a monstrance turning him into an abyssal tying Moray to him? Or turning him into an abyssal, offing him to gain that shard and exalting someone of his choice?*<br /> <br /> As it stands now Darktide could quit, he could be killed, he could be &quot;recruited&quot; by another deathlord etc. That is a seriously awesome resource that the Prince is gambling with there. Like Artifact N/A level resource he's gambling with there.<br /> <br /> *Disclaimer: Knowingly used previous edition concepts to help make a point/ask questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:20:08-07:00","id":911372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911369#post911369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The tricky thing there is that aside from a small handful, Solars have not been an overly prominent part of the setting in better than a thousand years. They've generally been hammered down almost as soon as they incarnate. It's explicitly because that restraint system is breaking down due to the impending dynastic struggle just as it's being made to deal with an unprecedented workload ten times larger than they'd previously been confronted with that the Solar Resurgence has been able to get its feet under it as a phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good point, and one I should have remembered as it's something I sometimes point out.<br /> <br /> So... I imagine that would be their view of Lunars. And broadly speaking, they'll treat Solars in a similar way. But it's a very new thing, so maybe it just hasn't come up yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:26:33-07:00","id":911375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911364#post911364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also now that you pointed out the harem I am profoundly disturbed/amused since I went back to the castebooks and it really does seem like he should be presence-supernal since he is literally attracting celestial exalts like flies... Is Darktide intentionally the protagonist of pirate-based harem anime?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Rakish Antihero Approach<br /> Cost:</b> -- (5m, 1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Presence 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Threefold Magnetic Ardor<br /> As the Solar presents himself as the seductive antihero, the world comes to love him. Whenever the Solar finds himself in combat with a named character of a heroic disposition whose Resolve is less than the Solar's Appearance, the Solar can activate this Charm at the end of the combat to create a minor intimacy of attraction between himself and the hero (as long as the hero is attracted to the Solar's gender, and has survived this combat). Should the Solar end an engagement he could have won and let his opponent leave on a draw, speaking of mysterious motives that are far too complex to glean and with an appreciative glance, the intimacy created is Major in strength.<br /> <br /> A heroic version of this Charm exists, and it is called <i>Bat and Cat Approach.</i><br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I regret nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:28:34-07:00","id":911376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911372#post911372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good point, and one I should have remembered as it's something I sometimes point out.<br /> <br /> So... I imagine that would be their view of Lunars. And broadly speaking, they'll treat Solars in a similar way. But it's a very new thing, so maybe it just hasn't come up yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always wondered why people so readily accepted Solars and Lunars as the same 'kind' of Anathema, their traits are literally night and day with little to nothing in common, aside from 'possession'. I understand particularly well-read monks knowing titles like 'defilers' and that they glow gold but most people should honestly think Lunar when they think Anathema and think what 'what the heck is that?' when they see a Solar with maybe the local priest/abbot thinking 'hmm... that golden glow seems like the demon-kings of ancient legends to me.' But not every townsmen or even government having an encyclopedic knowledge of how to identify the things that havent been seen for the most part in almost two millenia and their caste symbology when people cant even retain basic information from the Shogunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:29:19-07:00","id":911377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911375#post911375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Rakish Antihero Approach<br /> Cost:</b> -- (5m, 1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Presence 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Threefold Magnetic Ardor<br /> As the Solar presents himself as the seductive antihero, the world comes to love him. Whenever the Solar finds himself in combat with a named character of a heroic disposition whose Resolve is less than the Solar's Appearance, the Solar can activate this Charm at the end of the combat to create a minor intimacy of attraction between himself and the hero (as long as the hero is attracted to the Solar's gender, and has survived this combat). Should the Solar end an engagement he could have won and let his opponent leave on a draw, speaking of mysterious motives that are far too complex to glean and with an appreciative glance, the intimacy created is Major in strength.<br /> <br /> A heroic version of this Charm exists, and it is called <i>Bat and Cat Approach.</i><br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> I regret nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sir are a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:35:02-07:00","id":911380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911364#post911364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also now that you pointed out the harem I am profoundly disturbed/amused since I went back to the castebooks and it really does seem like he should be presence-supernal since he is literally attracting celestial exalts like flies... Is Darktide intentionally the protagonist of pirate-based harem anime?</div> </div> </div> </div>I regret that can't &quot;Like&quot; this more than once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:35:41-07:00","id":911382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911372#post911372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good point, and one I should have remembered as it's something I sometimes point out.<br /> <br /> So... I imagine that would be their view of Lunars. And broadly speaking, they'll treat Solars in a similar way. But it's a very new thing, so maybe it just hasn't come up yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. The Lunars have the Silver Pact some 300 Celestials strong working to rescue new exalts whenever possible, and pull them out of the Wyld Hunt's easy reach so that they can be trained and equipped to evade and/or fight it. Solars alternately have had none of that support structure, five percent of that number, roundabout, and an office of a global religion that actively uses divination to try and detect when new Solar exaltations are incoming, so that a murdersquad could be on hand to send them outgoing before they could do any damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:40:59-07:00","id":911384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911382#post911382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah. The Lunars have the Silver Pact some 300 Celestials strong working to rescue new exalts whenever possible, and pull them out of the Wyld Hunt's easy reach so that they can be trained and equipped to evade and/or fight it. Solars alternately have had none of that support structure, five percent of that number, roundabout, and an office of a global religion that actively uses divination to try and detect when new Solar exaltations are incoming, so that a murdersquad could be on hand to send them outgoing before they could do any damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone else have the feeling that the prediction method accidentally creates the circumstances for exaltation with a hilarious frequency in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:01:08-07:00","id":911398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911371#post911371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Moray Darktide but I have never understood this. Why in Creation would the Prince not throw Darktide in a monstrance turning him into an abyssal tying Moray to him? Or turning him into an abyssal, offing him to gain that shard and exalting someone of his choice?*</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever consider that maybe he <i>wants</i> a non-Abyssal? Or maybe he doesn't see a meaningful difference. Or maybe the Silver Prince isn't a super-god who can flip a switch on the divine fire inside you trivially, so either doesn't have the resources or doesn't wanna risk it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:02:28-07:00","id":911399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911398#post911398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever consider that maybe he <i>wants</i> a non-Abyssal? Or maybe he doesn't see a meaningful difference. Or maybe the Silver Prince isn't a super-god who can flip a switch on the divine fire inside you trivially, so either doesn't have the resources or doesn't wanna risk it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair the only time he tried this it was a catastrophic failure to the point that it is flat-out stated that he would never try it again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:03:26-07:00","id":911400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911384#post911384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone else have the feeling that the prediction method accidentally creates the circumstances for exaltation with a hilarious frequency in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sometimes, that may make for a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:12:49-07:00","id":911408,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Immaculate faith seperates Lunars and Solars, like how it has special understandings of Exigents. Like, clearly they are different (even an unlearned villager can spot the differnce between caste markings, for example). And while they are anathema, there are distinctions between fae and Solars. Maybe solars coming back is based on a different set of myths? To draw a real world example with some books of apochrypha: People know lunars as demonic horrors. Maybe people know solars as the ARCHdemonic horrors. The Asmodai to the Lunar's succubi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:27:35-07:00","id":911419,"title":"","content":"Oh, naturally. They simply use 'Anathema' where non-Immaculates' would use 'Exalt'. Solar Anathema, Lunar Anathema.... Technically, there's no lore on the Abyssal Exalted, because they're too new.. but it's likely that the Order is already throwing around the phrase 'Abyssal Anathema' at least informally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:34:22-07:00","id":911492,"title":"","content":"I think they're actually quite likely to refer to them as Solar Anathema. I mean, the Solars were trapped in the Underworld by Daana'd for 1500 years, of course some of them are death-aspected now. I wouldn't say they never differentiate between them, especially at the Dragon-blooded level, but I think most would go &quot;a black-armoured, blood-stained necromancer with the symbol of a bloody sun on their forehead? Sounds like a Solar to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyhow. They do seperate them, because the Immaculates actually have lists of Castes, like Frenzied, Wretched, Unclean, Moon-Mad, etc. Plus they know that the Moon Anathema have been fighting them for 1500 years while the Sun Anathema were trapped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:43:10-07:00","id":911494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911376#post911376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wondered why people so readily accepted Solars and Lunars as the same 'kind' of Anathema, their traits are literally night and day with little to nothing in common, aside from 'possession'. I understand particularly well-read monks knowing titles like 'defilers' and that they glow gold but most people should honestly think Lunar when they think Anathema and think what 'what the heck is that?' when they see a Solar with maybe the local priest/abbot thinking 'hmm... that golden glow seems like the demon-kings of ancient legends to me.' But not every townsmen or even government having an encyclopedic knowledge of how to identify the things that havent been seen for the most part in almost two millenia and their caste symbology when people cant even retain basic information from the Shogunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>True stuff. But if I were the Mouth of Peace and my loyal secretary (spoiler alert for those who may not know: in previous editions it was Chejop) informed me in RY 763 that the Solar anathema were making a comeback in a big way, oh, and by the way there are these black versions of them now, you can bet by RY 768 I'm going to have had the Immaculate Order spread that info as far and wide as frequently feasible so that the common person can inform us of the emergence of these vile anathema asap!<br /> <br /> I am the Mouth of Peace, and I approve this message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:46:16-07:00","id":911497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911492#post911492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're actually quite likely to refer to them as Solar Anathema. I mean, the Solars were trapped in the Underworld by Daana'd for 1500 years, of course some of them are death-aspected now. I wouldn't say they never differentiate between them, especially at the Dragon-blooded level, but I think most would go &quot;a black-armoured, blood-stained necromancer with the symbol of a bloody sun on their forehead? Sounds like a Solar to me.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound like a Solar, really. Not to any Dragon-Blooded officer that's ever actually been on Solar Detail in the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> The thing is... that's not something that the individuals actually engaging in the Hunt are likely to do, because a fair share of them (particularly Dragon-Blooded officers and Immaculate Monks) have seen and fought Solar Exalts, and they know the general patterns of their Anima Banners and Caste Marks. The concept of 'death-aspected Solar Anathema', whose Caste Markings are significantly different even if they're clearly reminiscent, and whose powers and proclivities are also very different warrants a separate classification. It's not in theme for a Solar Anathema to have charms to take the soldiers you threw against them and raise them as an undead horde to fight you. That would be in theme for a Death Knight. Death Knights have likely referred to themselves as Abyssal Exalted at various points, so the term 'Abyssal' is likely to filter into the Immaculate parlance via ground level and Sidereal level intelligence. A separate name for a separate classification of enemy is tactically valuable, while simply assuming 'Solars also come in goth now' makes communication with the military assets of the hunt needlessly unclear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:48:40-07:00","id":911499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911398#post911398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever consider that maybe he <i>wants</i> a non-Abyssal? Or maybe he doesn't see a meaningful difference. Or maybe the Silver Prince isn't a super-god who can flip a switch on the divine fire inside you trivially, so either doesn't have the resources or doesn't wanna risk it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I considered it. And in previous editions when the process didn't appear that complicated or costly for a deathlord and appeared to be a sure thing it still didn't make sense to me. Then again, I'm going off old memory and maybe there was a chance of a Solar shard escaping the monstrance instead of being converted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","user":"Darkon","date":". 06-10-2016, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:54:13-07:00","id":911500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911399#post911399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair the only time he tried this it was a catastrophic failure to the point that it is flat-out stated that he would never try it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right. Fallen Wolf of the Sea or some such. The Zenith who had uber zeal for life that the Prince broke in the monstrance and converted to almost a completely rebellious Midnight. I don't know...As loyal as Darktide is, he may go for it if just offered the opportunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T23:58:05-07:00","id":911503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911500#post911500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right. Fallen Wolf of the Sea or some such. The Zenith who had uber zeal for life that the Prince broke in the monstrance and converted to almost a completely rebellious Midnight. I don't know...As loyal as Darktide is, he may go for it if just offered the opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems doubtful. He rubs elbows with deathknights and knows what life is like as one. Some troubling quirks have no doubt made themselves noticed to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:05:35-07:00","id":911506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911398#post911398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ever consider that maybe he <i>wants</i> a non-Abyssal? Or maybe he doesn't see a meaningful difference. Or maybe the Silver Prince isn't a super-god who can flip a switch on the divine fire inside you trivially, so either doesn't have the resources or doesn't wanna risk it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The former seemed more likely to me. The Bodhisattva is first and foremost a head of state. Abyssals are hell on wheels for destroying things, but construction and development, cultivating new things... those aren't really in theme for them. Harder than one might think. Having a little diversity in the bullpen gives him access to options that can be valuable to him. <br /> <br /> He's also a Deathlord, and therefor by definition paranoid. If he's realized that there's a possibility that his Abyssal servants may one day try to supplant him, he'd probably be happy to have a Solar, capable of tapping anti-darkness powers, on payroll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:04:09-07:00","id":911579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911313#post911313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is to say that 'They are pragmatic about Solars but can work with them' applies to the entirety of the setting aside from the Realm and Lookshy. Making saying 'do we really need another place that is anti-Solars' ring very, very weird. From the the Perfect of Paragon to the Haslanti League to the Onyx Archipelago and to Halta, all those will tolerate and ally with Solars out of pragmatism. Sample NPCs from 1e all work on those various locations.<br /> <br /> Places that are 'pragmatic about Solars, but will work with them' are dime a dozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also depending on what canon you go by there's a lot of places that have serious issues with Dragon-Blooded.<br /> They're not allowed to go to Darkmist, Varang encourages them to fuck off, Halta sacrifices Fire Aspects because they might hurt the trees, I don't think the Haslanti League allows them to hold a position of authority either. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:09:49-07:00","id":911603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911579#post911579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Halta sacrifices Fire Aspects because they might hurt the trees</div> </div> </div> </div>While I know that traditions can often be pretty extreme, but isn't this a little too.....out there ? I feel like I'm reading fantasy PETA right now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:20:12-07:00","id":911606,"title":"","content":"That isn't nearly as bad as a fantasy version of PETA.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, let's put together a video to make people hate the fur industry!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sounds great! We can follow a fur trapper and film him catching a cute little seal and <i>skinning it alive!</i> That'll make people hate fur!&quot;<br /> &quot;Brilliant!&quot;<br /> ____<br /> &quot;So, I got word back from the fur trapper. Turns out they kill the animals before skinning them, because that's the practical <i>and</i> ethical way to do it. Maybe they're not the villainous chucklefucks we're painting them as\u2026&quot;<br /> &quot;We can't let something like <i>facts</i> get in the way of our mission! Just bribe him until he goes along with it!&quot;<br /> ____<br /> &quot;So, I got word back from the fur trapper. Turns out our little video netted him, like, a million pieces of hate mail, including death threats. He's gonna go to the public about us having bribed him.&quot;<br /> &quot;Fuck it, let's just make <a href=\"https://www.petakillsanimals.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/mommykills.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">gory cartoon pamphlets</a> full of propaganda about the fur industry, featuring cute little animals being murdered, and distribute them to elementary schools everywhere! Remind me to include bits telling the kids who'll read it <i>not to trust their parents if they wear fur</i>.&quot;<br /> &quot;Um\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> PETA is not ethical in its treatment of animals <i>or</i> humans, and most of their publicity stunts are a smokescreen to hide something <i>much</i> darker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-10-2016, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:42:29-07:00","id":911617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911229#post911229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even back in earliest 1e, in <i>Castebook: Zenith</i>, the Lookshy General Staff were getting ready to hunt down and kill their own decorated, honored veteran, and daughter of one of their own membership, Karal Fire Orchid, for Exalting as a Solar. You'd think that if they had ever had enough pragmatism to work with a Solar, &quot;The one who's a loyal Lookshyan soldier and the daughter of one of our general staff, who Exalted protecting a village from a Fair Folk raid&quot; would be the one they'd be like &quot;Sure, she doesn't sound so bad&quot; about.<br /> <br /> But no. Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems massively inaccurate, Stephen.<br /> <br /> I've always loved Karal Fire Orchid, but her writeup in Zenith doesn't bear a lot of resemblance to what you just described. The Lookshy General Staff doesn't actually <i>know </i>Fire Orchid is a Solar yet. That's a big plot point in her backstory, because it ties into her other big plot point, which is that her mother and brothers are, in fact, keeping an open mind about things; her brothers have been sent to find her, not to just murder her on sight, but because her family was like &quot;Okay, we <i>know</i> Fire Orchid, and she doesn't seem like the sort of person to make some sort of evil pact and steal power from the heavens, plus from what we can ascertain she's still being all heroic and shit. We're <i>hella</i> suspicious, and if it seems<i> at all </i>like she's become possessed by evil we're going to fucking end her, but first we're going to look her in the eye and hear what she has to say before we charge in with daiklaves swinging.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, people who aren't part of Gens Karal are probably not going to be that open-minded. Indeed, other members of Gens Karal who aren't specifically the progeny of Karal Linwei probably won't either. It's implied heavily that Fire Orchid's Exaltation is going to put a pin in Linwei's career no matter how this works out, and that the rest of the General Staff isn't going to be that pleased with her. But Linwei at least didn't just default to &quot;let's murder the Anathema,&quot; although I'll concede she probably would have if Fire Orchid weren't her kid.<br /> <br /> It seems like when it comes to Solars and Lookshy, the situation is going to be very contextual. As things stand normally, they're not going to want anything to do with the Solar Exalted, because they are strongly ideologically opposed to the Solars even existing, let alone entering into alliances or even non-aggression pacts with them.<br /> <br /> However, Lookshy is also a lot more practical about that than the Realm is. Nexus is only about, what, a week upriver from Lookshy, but Lookshy isn't going to try and invade and crush them for harboring large numbers of Anathema the way the Realm would any city-state in its own sphere of influence. If the Mask of Winters saddles up Dreadnought and heads for Lookshy surrounded by a massive corpse-army and his entire Abyssal honor guard in kickass bonestriders, the General Staff may stroke their chins and <i>seriously</i> consider the offer if Dace shows up with <i>his</i> army and is like &quot;You guys want to team up against the terrible unlife abominations?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's all contextual. But as a matter of the &quot;status quo&quot; you probably don't have an in, because the Lookshyans still take their faith <i>very</i> seriously and their faith says &quot;if it glows gold, kill it.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right. Fallen Wolf of the Sea or some such. The Zenith who had uber zeal for life that the Prince broke in the monstrance and converted to almost a completely rebellious Midnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, I believe that Fallen Wolf has actually begun manifesting Solar essence again (in the form of being able to use his essence in the way Solars do, that is, using Solar Charms) and it is implied he's <i>this</i> close to becoming a Solar again, which would mean that the Bodhisvatta spent a ton of time and effort on him to end up in a place worse than he was before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:56:33-07:00","id":911622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911617#post911617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Mask of Winters saddles up Dreadnought and heads for Lookshy\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreadnought_%28comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">I'm down with that image, too.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911617#post911617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026surrounded by a massive corpse-army and his entire Abyssal honor guard in kickass bonestriders\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Confirmed by the Ex3 devs: No fuckstriders, bonestriders, or striderstriders.<br /> <br /> Re: Karal Linwei: Just because people believe in an Abrahamic religion doesn't mean that they will necessarily tie their only child to a rock and start stabbing because they started hearing voices in their heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-10-2016, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:03:09-07:00","id":911625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911579#post911579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not allowed to go to Darkmist, Varang encourages them to fuck off, Halta sacrifices Fire Aspects because they might hurt the trees, I don't think the Haslanti League allows them to hold a position of authority either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 90% sure the Haslanti have an Outcaste airboat captain. They just don't give them positions of special privilege out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:56:46-07:00","id":911652,"title":"","content":"This may seem surprising, but maybe when people are confronted by a soul-eating demon bent on world domination, it's possible they act like they are confronting a demon?<br /> <br /> Whenever I read &quot;Well, they are Anathema, but...&quot; I smell metagaming. OC, we know Celestials aren't Anathema. But nobody in Creation has a copy of the core book sitting on their shelf. They know only what the Immaculates tell them. And the Immaculates tell them the Anathema are evil.<br /> <br /> This is one reason why Lunars and Solars tend to build their followings from the oppressed and the marginalized. Those people are desperate enough to think serving/allying with an Anathema is worth a shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo 06-10-2016, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:31:59-07:00","id":911674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911622#post911622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreadnought_%28comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">I'm down with that image, too.</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh. I meant, of course, Juggernaut. Dreadnought? How did I get there?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Confirmed by the Ex3 devs: No fuckstriders, bonestriders, or striderstriders. </div> </div> </div>... do they just mean the <i>term </i>is going away, or the actual <i>objects</i>?<br /> <br /> Because if I can't hook my Abyssals up with the necrotic equivalent of warstriders then I can't even. The idea that the Underworld and Malfeas both have their own flavors of crazy war machines is an excellent one, why the hell would you move away from that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may seem surprising, but maybe when people are confronted by a soul-eating demon bent on world domination, it's possible they act like they are confronting a demon?</div> </div> </div> </div>And some people will notice that supposed soul-eating demon bent on world domination isn't acting at all like either a soul-eater, a demon, or a conqueror, and maybe they'll exercise some critical thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whenever I read &quot;Well, they are Anathema, but...&quot; I smell metagaming. OC, we know Celestials aren't Anathema. But nobody in Creation has a copy of the core book sitting on their shelf. They know only what the Immaculates tell them. And the Immaculates tell them the Anathema are evil. </div> </div> </div>Lots of people in Creation live in places where the Immaculate Philosophy isn't the state religion.<br /> <br /> Many people who <i>do</i> live in places where the Immaculate Philosophy is the state religion or at least massively state-supported will observe the fact that the Immaculate Order is robustly committed to making them all utterly subservient to the Dragon-Blooded while reaping all the wealth from their lands to send to the Blessed Isle, and they'll start to question if they should accept uncritically everything it says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:39:51-07:00","id":911680,"title":"","content":"This is what Intimacies are for. If your ties to your sibling is strong than your faith in the Immaculate Texts, then you may start second guessing your religion. <br /> <br /> I'm also not a big fan of limiting character concepts. If a player wants to play a Dragonblooded character with a Solar Sibling, I'm going to let them. I'm going to explain that the character will be doing what society says is wrong, etc and to consider that in their character concept. If it doesn't break the game I want to run, then I won't deny the concept out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:06:27-07:00","id":911701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911617#post911617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems massively inaccurate, Stephen.<br /> <br /> I've always loved Karal Fire Orchid, but her writeup in Zenith doesn't bear a lot of resemblance to what you just described. The Lookshy General Staff doesn't actually <i>know </i>Fire Orchid is a Solar yet. That's a big plot point in her backstory, because it ties into her other big plot point, which is that her mother and brothers are, in fact, keeping an open mind about things; her brothers have been sent to find her, not to just murder her on sight, but because her family was like &quot;Okay, we <i>know</i> Fire Orchid, and she doesn't seem like the sort of person to make some sort of evil pact and steal power from the heavens, plus from what we can ascertain she's still being all heroic and shit. We're <i>hella</i> suspicious, and if it seems<i> at all </i>like she's become possessed by evil we're going to fucking end her, but first we're going to look her in the eye and hear what she has to say before we charge in with daiklaves swinging.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How could the General Staff not know? The Intelligence directorate had those reports on hand in the &quot;Voices Not Our Own&quot; section for Gens Karal - that was even how her family found out in the first place. It's not difficult for another taimyo to requisition them, learn the same information, connect the dots, and talk to other members of the General Staff. To top it off, there are entire villages full of people willing to loudly and proudly proclaim it to anyone who passed through. There is no secret identity going on here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, people who aren't part of Gens Karal are probably not going to be that open-minded. Indeed, other members of Gens Karal who aren't specifically the progeny of Karal Linwei probably won't either. It's implied heavily that Fire Orchid's Exaltation is going to put a pin in Linwei's career no matter how this works out, and that the rest of the General Staff isn't going to be that pleased with her. But Linwei at least didn't just default to &quot;let's murder the Anathema,&quot; although I'll concede she probably would have if Fire Orchid weren't her kid.<br /> <br /> It seems like when it comes to Solars and Lookshy, the situation is going to be very contextual. As things stand normally, they're not going to want anything to do with the Solar Exalted, because they are strongly ideologically opposed to the Solars even existing, let alone entering into alliances or even non-aggression pacts with them.<br /> <br /> However, Lookshy is also a lot more practical about that than the Realm is. Nexus is only about, what, a week upriver from Lookshy, but Lookshy isn't going to try and invade and crush them for harboring large numbers of Anathema the way the Realm would any city-state in its own sphere of influence. If the Mask of Winters saddles up Dreadnought and heads for Lookshy surrounded by a massive corpse-army and his entire Abyssal honor guard in kickass bonestriders, the General Staff may stroke their chins and <i>seriously</i> consider the offer if Dace shows up with <i>his</i> army and is like &quot;You guys want to team up against the terrible unlife abominations?&quot; </div> </div> </div>You'd better hope it isn't Dace that shows up; his circle agreed to a non-aggression pact with the Mask. They even had Swan seal it with an oath. Can't trust those damned Solar Anathema, right?<br /> <br /> Now, they might invite back some of their own who went glowing off the reservation, but it's going to be a strictly temporary thing under most circumstances. They won't get to move back in, or rejoin their family, or anything of the sort. They probably will get only surveillance and not any death squads pinned on them in the future, so long as the benign neglect doesn't eventually turn up dirty laundry.<br /> <br /> (Topic change - bonestriders going on the pile)<br /> <br /> It's the term, mostly, I think. You aren't going to make anything on par with a warstrider just by lashing together bones and sinews; at best, that would be like a piloted version of the automaton/walking statue QC. You need a huge amount of soulsteel and someone who can make Artifact N/As, because all warstriders are Artifact N/As, no matter their status as divine, hellish, or macabre. The skulls would be purely for decoration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:14:34-07:00","id":911707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911701#post911701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How could the General Staff not know? The Intelligence directorate had those reports on hand in the &quot;Voices Not Our Own&quot; section for Gens Karal - that was even how her family found out in the first place. It's not difficult for another taimyo to requisition them, learn the same information, connect the dots, and talk to other members of the General Staff. To top it off, there are entire villages full of people willing to loudly and proudly proclaim it to anyone who passed through. There is no secret identity going on here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You'd better hope it isn't Dace that shows up; his circle agreed to a non-aggression pact with the Mask. They even had Swan seal it with an oath. Can't trust those damned Solar Anathema, right?<br /> <br /> Now, they might invite back some of their own who went glowing off the reservation, but it's going to be a strictly temporary thing under most circumstances. They won't get to move back in, or rejoin their family, or anything of the sort. They probably will get only surveillance and not any death squads pinned on them in the future, so long as the benign neglect doesn't eventually turn up dirty laundry.<br /> <br /> (Topic change - bonestriders going on the pile)<br /> <br /> It's the term, mostly, I think. You aren't going to make anything on par with a warstrider just by lashing together bones and sinews; at best, that would be like a piloted version of the automaton/walking statue QC. You need a huge amount of soulsteel and someone who can make Artifact N/As, because all warstriders are Artifact N/As, no matter their status as divine, hellish, or macabre. The skulls would be purely for decoration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone ever think that the canon Solars seem to mostly exist to be a nuissance which generally just complicate things for competent PC/NPCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:52:38-07:00","id":911724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911707#post911707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone ever think that the canon Solars seem to mostly exist to be a nuissance which generally just complicate things for competent PC/NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unless you play them, that's generally how they turn out, right? Short of declaring them to not exist, there's not much avoiding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:00:35-07:00","id":911726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911707#post911707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone ever think that the canon Solars seem to mostly exist to be a nuissance which generally just complicate things for competent PC/NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I just ignore the Canon Solars in a Solar game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:09:18-07:00","id":911732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911707#post911707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone ever think that the canon Solars seem to mostly exist to be a nuissance which generally just complicate things for competent PC/NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Signature characters in 1e were meant to serve as examples of the sort of things your PCs could get up to, not setting elements you had to maneuver around. Or, at least, that's how they were optimized, hence the MoW non-aggression pact (&quot;Just because Skeletor is right there doesn't mean the PCs <i>have</i> to fight him&quot;). Some books treated them as setting elements, obviously, but you've identified the problem with that -- <i>as </i>setting elements, they're kinda shitty setting elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:25:53-07:00","id":911747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911732#post911732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Signature characters in 1e were meant to serve as examples of the sort of things your PCs could get up to, not setting elements you had to maneuver around. Or, at least, that's how they were optimized, hence the MoW non-aggression pact (&quot;Just because Skeletor is right there doesn't mean the PCs <i>have</i> to fight him&quot;). Some books treated them as setting elements, obviously, but you've identified the problem with that -- <i>as </i>setting elements, they're kinda shitty setting elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly meant it as an amusing observation, I generally like alot of the characters (Sayn and Avaku (cant recall if that is the proper spelling) being some personal favourites of mine) from the castebooks and think that they add to the world since I am not very fond of the 'only notable/competent Solar characters are the PCs' approach. <br /> <br /> I do note that the 'main' circle tended towards being shockingly incompetent compared to most other 'main' characters from other splats and even other castebook Solars though. (Since they get tricked/captured/manipulated and seem to never do anything productive in comparison). This is something I hope they avert in 3rd, the main circle can be interesting wothout stealig the spotlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 06-10-2016, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:27:23-07:00","id":911748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911625#post911625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm 90% sure the Haslanti have an Outcaste airboat captain. They just don't give them positions of special privilege out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean airboat captains, but the bit in Compass North saying something to that effect it also tells us that despite being considered heroes &quot;they must work for respect and prove their patriotism over and over again&quot; suggesting there's a bit of a glass ceiling even for their home grown Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:19:55-07:00","id":911776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911674#post911674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... do they just mean the <i>term </i>is going away, or the actual <i>objects</i>?<br /> <br /> Because if I can't hook my Abyssals up with the necrotic equivalent of warstriders then I can't even. The idea that the Underworld and Malfeas both have their own flavors of crazy war machines is an excellent one, why the hell would you move away from that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it non-figuratively made warstriders less special. Also, as alien as Malfeas and the Underworld <i>are</i>, you're telling me the best war-machines the Princes of Hell and the Lords of the Dead could come up with is... green and bone palette-swaps of regular warstriders?<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you know what I <i>don't </i>object to? Abyssals having warstriders. Not bonestriders. Warstriders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:21:08-07:00","id":911816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911622#post911622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confirmed by the Ex3 devs: No fuckstriders</div> </div> </div> </div>You take that back right now.<br /> <br /> If I can't play a Chosen of Serenity in a Blue Fuckstrider, I'm quitting Exalted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","user":"EmanantVolition","date":". 06-10-2016, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:43:45-07:00","id":911827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911816#post911816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You take that back right now.<br /> <br /> If I can't play a Chosen of Serenity in a Blue Fuckstrider, I'm quitting Exalted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>We already wrote everything we could think of about fuckstriders in 2e. We have no more fuckstriders to give.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:57:50-07:00","id":911830,"title":"","content":"So, what I am curious about, is whether or not in 3rd edition you can make artifacts out of materials that aren't the Five Magical Materials. Or can artifacts <i>only</i> be made out of those materials? Could you make a daiklave out of the bones of an ancient behemoth and quenched in the blood of a third circle demon? Or would it have to incorporate one of the five magical material somewhere in it as well?<br /> <br /> As 2nd edition progressed we got new materials that you could construct artifacts out of. Is that idea still in 3rd edition, or is it &quot;5 Magical Materials Only?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:05:03-07:00","id":911834,"title":"","content":"I think that's still the case (I remember a quote but can't find it), but they might not get nailed down effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:13:30-07:00","id":911839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911579#post911579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also depending on what canon you go by there's a lot of places that have serious issues with Dragon-Blooded.<br /> They're not allowed to go to Darkmist, Varang encourages them to fuck off, <b>Halta sacrifices Fire Aspects because they might hurt the trees</b>, I don't think the Haslanti League allows them to hold a position of authority either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangential, but this is a pet peeve of mine since it was pointed out to me. Redwood conifer forests <i>want </i>fire to reproduce, it's vital to the cycles of their forest and keeping &quot;lesser&quot; plantlife from growing too large and threatening the great trees. Fire Aspects should be welcomed in Halta because their precious trees are fire resistant and the trees of their enemies <i>are not</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:16:46-07:00","id":911878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911229#post911229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even back in earliest 1e, in <i>Castebook: Zenith</i>, the Lookshy General Staff were getting ready to hunt down and kill their own decorated, honored veteran, and daughter of one of their own membership, Karal Fire Orchid, for Exalting as a Solar. You'd think that if they had ever had enough pragmatism to work with a Solar, &quot;The one who's a loyal Lookshyan soldier and the daughter of one of our general staff, who Exalted protecting a village from a Fair Folk raid&quot; would be the one they'd be like &quot;Sure, she doesn't sound so bad&quot; about.<br /> <br /> But no. Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then 2E, in a shocking moment, actually saw a dynamic there and did not, in fact, make it Edgier. IIRC, in the Scroll of Exalts, Linwei wanted to use political influence to ensure that she got to see Fire Orchid herself, with her own two eyes, to judge for herself whether her daughter was a monster, or still her daughter.<br /> <br /> So, y'know, conflict and so much chance for character dynamics. And I love that more than what the 1E writeup sounds like it's portraying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:55:53-07:00","id":911916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911674#post911674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some people will notice that supposed soul-eating demon bent on world domination isn't acting at all like either a soul-eater, a demon, or a conqueror, and maybe they'll exercise some critical thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite right. The demon will act kind, human, vulnerable. The demon will offer to use its power to help you, and will seem to be a great hero with all the best intentions. And thus the Exalt will act exactly in accordance with everything the average person has been taught about Anathema.<br /> <br /> Let's put it another way. I tell you the dog in my backyard likes to act friendly, and then bites out of nowhere, tries to pull you down to the ground, and goes for your face. The dog weighs damn near two hundred pounds. You go outside and the dog runs up, tail wagging, tongue lolling, and begs to be pet. Do you exercise &quot;critical thought&quot; and pet the dog, because clearly he's a nice puppy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:35:19-07:00","id":911926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911916#post911916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's put it another way. I tell you the dog in my backyard likes to act friendly, and then bites out of nowhere, tries to pull you down to the ground, and goes for your face. The dog weighs damn near two hundred pounds. You go outside and the dog runs up, tail wagging, tongue lolling, and begs to be pet. Do you exercise &quot;critical thought&quot; and pet the dog, because clearly he's a nice puppy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would :&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:36:17-07:00","id":911928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911776#post911776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, you know what I <i>don't </i>object to? Abyssals having warstriders. Not bonestriders. Warstriders.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if I'm an Abyssal, and I look at Juggernaut and go &quot;fuck me, I want a warstrider version of THAT!&quot;<br /> <br /> Because it seems like that should be not only doable, but desirable. The Abyssals shouldn't be using the same warstriders everyone else are. They should be piloting terrifying damned monstrosities made of blood and bone and ash, powered by souls.<br /> <br /> I utterly don't buy this &quot;they make warstriders less special&quot; nonsense. Do the Cryxian bonejacks in Warmachine make Cygnaran warjacks less special? They do not.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The demon will act kind, human, vulnerable. The demon will offer to use its power to help you, and will seem to be a great hero with all the best intentions. And thus the Exalt will act exactly in accordance with everything the average person has been taught about Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this actually Immaculate doctrine with regard to the Solar and Lunar Anathema?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's put it another way. I tell you the dog in my backyard likes to act friendly, and then bites out of nowhere, tries to pull you down to the ground, and goes for your face. </div> </div> </div><i>My</i> reaction would be &quot;dogs don't behave like that. They don't bite 'out of nowhere.' Either that animal has been abused in a way that causes it to attack based off a trigger that's otherwise innocuous, or it's been TRAINED to attack off a trigger that's otherwise innocuous. What the fuck have you been doing to that poor animal?&quot;<br /> <br /> Some other people might take you at your word, though, because they're ignorant of dogs and how they behave. That doesn't make them wrong. That just means they trusted you when they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Plenty of people are going to totally buy the Immaculate line on the Anathema. But some people are not. Because they don't trust the Immaculate Order. Because they think &quot;well that's a mighty fine catch-22 you've constructed with regard to the Anathema, isn't it? REAL fine, that catch-22. Especially the part where you demand we give you all our jade to protect us from them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:39:32-07:00","id":911930,"title":"","content":"Why don't Abyssals get their own special bone versions of daiklaves?<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you want a warstrider in the image of Juggernaut, then make a warstrider in the image of Juggernaut.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:40:46-07:00","id":911932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911928#post911928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I'm an Abyssal, and I look at Juggernaut and go &quot;fuck me, I want a warstrider version of THAT!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you build a Warstrider version of that out of bone and enjoy your new Warstrider, I would think. I certainly don't think the devs intend for you to never make a warstrider out of bone and flesh and magical material, it's just a poorly-communicated change of terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11456-nihnoz","name":"nihnoz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11456_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:49:21-07:00","id":911937,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of different levels of Immaculate doctrine re: Anathema. The lowest level is &quot;You don't need to know anything except that if you see one, go see a priest.&quot; Somewhere in the middle is &quot;More than any other factor, the pride that motivates one to step outside one's position in the Immaculate Hierarchy is what invites Anathemic possession. Even the best, most kind and magnanimous person in the world can become an Anathema, her soul forfeit, if her kindness and magnaminity motivates her to try too mightily to rise above her station and bend the world to her own whims and conscience rather than the wisdom of her betters.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T15:58:07-07:00","id":911944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911928#post911928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What if I'm an Abyssal, and I look at Juggernaut and go &quot;fuck me, I want a warstrider version of THAT!&quot;<br /> <br /> Because it seems like that should be not only doable, but desirable. The Abyssals shouldn't be using the same warstriders everyone else are. They should be piloting terrifying damned monstrosities made of blood and bone and ash, powered by souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess, off hand, you could probably still make a Warstrider out of the bones of a behemoth and covered in soulsteel runes which scream hymns to the Neverborn. <br /> <br /> But it's not a &quot;bonestrider,&quot; it's just a Warstrider that happens to have used bones in its construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:14:46-07:00","id":912016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911930#post911930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't Abyssals get their own special bone versions of daiklaves?</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>do</i> get their very own magical materiel that's specifically in-theme for them and has it's own special name, tho. They're not just all using orichalcum. There's also a specifically death-inflected version of sorcery that is largely their purview, which, hey, gets its own special name as well!<br /> <br /> You will note that my immediate follow-up question to Alucard was &quot;is it the thing <i>itself </i>which is going away, or is just the<i> term </i>that's going away?&quot; I'm not particularly attached to the term &quot;bonejack&quot;, although I do think both &quot;bonejack&quot; and &quot;helljack&quot; are pretty cool terms. I <i>am</i> attached to the idea that the warstriders piloted by the vanguards of the Underworld who seek to propagate the Chivalry of Death probably should not just be the same sort of warstriders the Realm or Lookshy has.<br /> <br /> When I think of the sort of warstrider a Dragon-Blood or Solar might be piloting, I think of Escaflowne or possibly some species of Gundam or Knightmare. Those do not seem... appropriate for Abyssals, although one imagines they're perfectly capable of piloting them if they so choose. But when I think Abyssal warstrider, I'm thinking some terrifying agglomeration of soulsteel and bone and necrotic power that oozes ichor and blood. Something that could be on the cover of a death metal album.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":4742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","user":"Murcushio","date":". 06-10-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:35:32-07:00","id":912028,"title":"","content":"Did I say orichalcum warstriders? Where? Where did I say that? Why would I say Abyssals have to use orichalcum warstriders?<br /> <br /> The term and the idea that a warstrider made of bones and soulsteel being sufficiently different from other kinds of warstriders as to need its own distinct classification, both those notions are going away, is my understanding. After all, the designations of &quot;warstrider classes&quot; had been done away with as well, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:41:47-07:00","id":912032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912016#post912016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They <i>do</i> get their very own magical materiel that's specifically in-theme for them and has it's own special name, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly; they don't need a special necrotic version that gets its own kind of name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I think of the sort of warstrider a Dragon-Blood or Solar might be piloting, I think of Escaflowne or possibly some species of Gundam or Knightmare. Those do not seem... appropriate for Abyssals, although one imagines they're perfectly capable of piloting them if they so choose. But when I think Abyssal warstrider, I'm thinking some terrifying agglomeration of soulsteel and bone and necrotic power that oozes ichor and blood. Something that could be on the cover of a death metal album.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bA bit like the sky cutter in the core?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:43:39-07:00","id":912033,"title":"","content":"Bonestrider, Necromancy, Dragon of a different colors, Necrotech. Are there a reasons why Abyssal has so much &quot;Our own toy&quot; compare to other splat ? Is it because they are goth and thus don't use mainstream things ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:44:00-07:00","id":912035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912016#post912016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not particularly attached to the term &quot;bonejack&quot;, although I do think both &quot;bonejack&quot; and &quot;helljack&quot; are pretty cool terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, every time I came across the term &quot;bonejack&quot; it made me giggle like I was back in 3rd grade. I'll miss the term for its unintentional comedic value, but I really hope I don't see it again in 3rd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T18:45:04-07:00","id":912036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911674#post911674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... do they just mean the <i>term </i>is going away, or the actual <i>objects</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>More the term.<br /> Much as there's nothing stopping you from forging a daiklave from a behemoth's tooth rather than a magic material you can create warstriders from whatever materials you and your ST deems suitable and cool enough. Having the Bonestrider be its own category gives the impression it\u2019s a Soulsteel Warstrider on a budget (which is impressive given that Deathlords seem to shit the stuff) rather than building your warmachine around a behemoth corpse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:23:09-07:00","id":912045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912033#post912033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonestrider, Necromancy, Dragon of a different colors, Necrotech. Are there a reasons why Abyssal has so much &quot;Our own toy&quot; compare to other splat ? Is it because they are goth and thus don't use mainstream things ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A chapter on the special necrotech artifacts of the underworld that get their own special mechanics is an easier back-of-the-book promotional sales point than a chapter on more artifacts, except they're underworld-y. Same with helltech, hence an entire chapter in Infernals filled with the rules for hellforged wonders instead of e.g. an entire chapter filled with artifacts that happen to be hell-y.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're doing that this edition. We don't need artifacts, and then also necrotech artifacts that use a different set of mechanics from artifacts, and then also hellforged wonders/helltech that uses a different set of mechanics from artifacts and necrotech artifacts. Likewise, the number of warstriders in the setting is being vastly reduced and the subcategorization of warstriders into scout/[whatever the other two categories are, I can't remember] is going away, so why would we keep an entirely separate category of warstrider-like-things that behave like warstriders but aren't called warstriders because they're all death-flavored?<br /> <br /> Bonestriders are almost certainly going away for a number of reasons that fit together like Lego pieces:<br /> <br /> 1) The number of warstrider-like-things in the setting is being reduced; bonestriders themselves were always sold as &quot;cheaper, mass-produced-by-necrotech Underworld warstrider equivalents,&quot; but since we're removing mass-produced artifact-type-stuff from the setting as a rule, the inclusion of bonestriders would seem not to be in line with that.<br /> <br /> 2) The profusion of superfluous types of artifacts with their own custom creation and maintenance mechanics is also being pared down, because they never served a strong purpose other than to sell people books on the promise of, not just new toys, but entirely new categories of toys.<br /> <br /> You can still have a giant robot made of skulls and metal forged from screaming souls, obviously. It's just be &quot;a warstrider.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T19:58:05-07:00","id":912052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912045#post912045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A chapter on the special necrotech artifacts of the underworld that get their own special mechanics is an easier back-of-the-book promotional sales point than a chapter on more artifacts, except they're underworld-y. Same with helltech, hence an entire chapter in Infernals filled with the rules for hellforged wonders instead of e.g. an entire chapter filled with artifacts that happen to be hell-y.<br /> <br /> I don't think we're doing that this edition. We don't need artifacts, and then also necrotech artifacts that use a different set of mechanics from artifacts, and then also hellforged wonders/helltech that uses a different set of mechanics from artifacts and necrotech artifacts. Likewise, the number of warstriders in the setting is being vastly reduced and the subcategorization of warstriders into scout/[whatever the other two categories are, I can't remember] is going away, so why would we keep an entirely separate category of warstrider-like-things that behave like warstriders but aren't called warstriders because they're all death-flavored?<br /> <br /> Bonestriders are almost certainly going away for a number of reasons that fit together like Lego pieces:<br /> <br /> 1) The number of warstrider-like-things in the setting is being reduced; bonestriders themselves were always sold as &quot;cheaper, mass-produced-by-necrotech Underworld warstrider equivalents,&quot; but since we're removing mass-produced artifact-type-stuff from the setting as a rule, the inclusion of bonestriders would seem not to be in line with that.<br /> <br /> 2) The profusion of superfluous types of artifacts with their own custom creation and maintenance mechanics is also being pared down, because they never served a strong purpose other than to sell people books on the promise of, not just new toys, but entirely new categories of toys.<br /> <br /> You can still have a giant robot made of skulls and metal forged from screaming souls, obviously. It's just be &quot;a warstrider.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved necrotech oddly enough, not the actual necromantic artifacts (those tended to be rather boring and unneeded) but the make-a-monster workshop that you could use to make necrosurgery/crafting fun and interesting. I am still amused when I recall the time someone in my group decided to make the suit from Crysis out of actual muscles and ligaments for his cultists. Not to mention it was entertainingly campy in an otherwise pointlessly dark book. And I dont think anyone I played with ever actually used a necrotech artifact instead of just making a fun new minion/war-machine woth the closest thing being the warrior-suits for cultists. <br /> <br /> Now alternative systems for making what could be accomplished with normal crafting? Not really necessary at all I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:40:06-07:00","id":912082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912016#post912016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They <i>do</i> get their very own magical materiel that's specifically in-theme for them and has it's own special name, tho. They're not just all using orichalcum. There's also a specifically death-inflected version of sorcery that is largely their purview, which, hey, gets its own special name as well!<br /> <br /> You will note that my immediate follow-up question to Alucard was &quot;is it the thing <i>itself </i>which is going away, or is just the<i> term </i>that's going away?&quot; I'm not particularly attached to the term &quot;bonejack&quot;, although I do think both &quot;bonejack&quot; and &quot;helljack&quot; are pretty cool terms. I <i>am</i> attached to the idea that the warstriders piloted by the vanguards of the Underworld who seek to propagate the Chivalry of Death probably should not just be the same sort of warstriders the Realm or Lookshy has.<br /> <br /> When I think of the sort of warstrider a Dragon-Blood or Solar might be piloting, I think of Escaflowne or possibly some species of Gundam or Knightmare. Those do not seem... appropriate for Abyssals, although one imagines they're perfectly capable of piloting them if they so choose. But when I think Abyssal warstrider, I'm thinking some terrifying agglomeration of soulsteel and bone and necrotic power that oozes ichor and blood. Something that could be on the cover of a death metal album.</div> </div> </div> </div>You sort that out with soulsteel-appropriate powers and Evocations, not a completely different set of construction rules or class of Artifact. Soul Mirror is definitely different from Beloved Adorei or or Volcano Cutter. You don't even need to make necromancy its own thing, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:12:48-07:00","id":912163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912036#post912036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having the Bonestrider be its own category gives the impression it\u2019s a Soulsteel Warstrider on a budget.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also difficult to disassociate them from the Warstriders you can summon into being with Rattled Bones of War.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:16:20-07:00","id":912295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911930#post911930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't Abyssals get their own special bone versions of daiklaves?<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Abyssals get their own special 'forged from ghosts in a horrific torturous process' versions of Daiklaves instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:18:33-07:00","id":912297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912295#post912295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Abyssals get their own special 'forged from ghosts in a horrific torturous process' versions of Daiklaves instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, not really. Anyone can get those. Also, regardless, it's still ultimately a daiklave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T10:35:13-07:00","id":912303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912297#post912297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, not really. Anyone can get those. Also, regardless, it's still ultimately a daiklave.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the downside of the new 'open range' policy on Artifacts. It kind of intrudes into niche protection.... Still, one would expect that soulsteel artifacts will still resonate with Abyssals, and Abyssals should properly be dripping with the stuff, what with having access to the armories of the Deathlords, and being their champions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:00:48-07:00","id":912318,"title":"","content":"What niche was entailed by necrotech and bonestriders?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:47:32-07:00","id":912353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912295#post912295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because Abyssals get their own special 'forged from ghosts in a horrific torturous process' versions of Daiklaves instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, many Abyssal artifacts probably are made out of bones and soulsteel and sinew and such, just like they were in First Edition, years before the term &quot;necrotech&quot; was ever introduced into the gameline. Back then, if an artifact was made out of bones and screaming ghosts and looked like something off the cover of an Iron Maiden album, it was called an &quot;artifact.&quot; That's how it will work in 3rd edition. <br /> <br /> Abyssals (and Infernals) will still have their same cool niche for artifacts made out of left-over body parts and demons, it's just that the process for making those sorts of artifacts won't be getting special snowflake treatment, being called something different and given their own special subsystem for making them.<br /> <br /> What this means is that, yes in Third Edition if a Solar or a Dragon Blooded wanted to make a suit of armor out of screaming souls and bone and sinew, they can. But they could always do this in First Edition and they could do this in Second Edition. The only difference was that they needed to use a totally different subsystem for making such a device than for making the (mechanically) exact same artifact out of different materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:52:41-07:00","id":912357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912318#post912318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What niche was entailed by necrotech and bonestriders?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main value of Necrotech was the ability to make warbeasts and units in a quick and easy manner for necromancers, Bonestriders arguably served no real purpose that a giant made of bones couldnt fill since they were mostly meant for minor NPCs while Abyssals rode soulsteel warstriders. In 3rd bonestriders arent really needed (except for a unique one from behemoth bones) while you could still use necrotech if you ditched the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:07:56-07:00","id":912369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912357#post912357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main value of Necrotech was the ability to make warbeasts and units in a quick and easy manner for necromancers, Bonestriders arguably served no real purpose that a giant made of bones couldnt fill since they were mostly meant for minor NPCs while Abyssals rode soulsteel warstriders. In 3rd bonestriders arent really needed (except for a unique one from behemoth bones) while you could still use necrotech if you ditched the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a &quot;Build-A-Bearbeast&quot; system could be quite cool and useful in Third Edition, just that the system should apply equally to making spinechains, creating Wyld Behemoths, constructing clockwork servitors and breeding six-legged horses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-11-2016, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:08:45-07:00","id":912370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912318#post912318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What niche was entailed by necrotech and bonestriders?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't referring to that particular niche. I was referring to the general 'Exalt type to Magical Material' correspondence. The fact that Abyssals were the group most fundamentally comfortable with wearing armor and wielding weapons made from screaming tormented souls said something meaningful about their themes. With those materials now potentially open to other exalt types, that theme is in danger of being diluted. Note that I say 'in danger of', not 'presently being', because there's still plenty of room for good and dedicated writing to refine and reinforce those themes while still allowing the new broader artifact usage rules to stand. The policy of no longer allowing mass produced artifacts to be a thing should assist with that a great deal.<br /> <br /> By the way, AnubisXy? Everything you just said both just now and in response to me explicitly? I'm all for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:56:40-07:00","id":912393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912369#post912369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a &amp;quot;Build-A-Bearbeast&amp;quot; system could be quite cool and useful in Third Edition, just that the system should apply equally to making spinechains, creating Wyld Behemoths, constructing clockwork servitors and breeding six-legged horses.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be even better to be frank, I am just fond of the point-build systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:24:45-07:00","id":912405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912370#post912370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he fact that Abyssals were the group most fundamentally comfortable with wearing armor and wielding weapons made from screaming tormented souls said something meaningful about their themes. With those materials now potentially open to other exalt types, that theme is in danger of being diluted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect with the new rules you're more likely to see Deathknights branching out and using other magical items than the reverse (and for very good reason, screaming swords have their drawbacks.)<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters sat on his massive throne, carved from the blackest basalt and decorated with the countless skulls of his fallen enemies. There, in his fortress atop the Juggernaut, surrounded by a legion of his finest soldiers and most trusted advisers, his power was at its peak. In front of him knelt one of his Deathknights.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ahh, Unending Darkness of the Final Day. Of all of my followers, you are among the most loyal. You repeatedly demonstrate initiative and wisdom, engaging in tasks for the benefit of Thorns and myself. You have even repeatedly helped your fellow Deathknights. Indeed, you are one of my finest and darkest gems. You may rise and explain to me, for what reason have you come before me this day.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unending Darkness slowly stood. His gaze turned, taking in the vast array of ghostly soldiers and the gallery of onlookers whose only task, it seemed, was to make the Mask of Winters more imposing and fearsome. Finally his gaze turned to the Deathlord. &quot;My master. It is with great regret that I come to ask you for a new daiklave.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters froze, and as he did, so too did all of the gathered watchers in the vast chambers. &quot;A new daiklave?&quot; The ancient and terrible witch-king asked slowly. &quot;And just what happened to the one I gave you?&quot;<br /> <br /> The deathknight furtively looked around and then pulled out a sheathed sword. &quot;It is here my lord.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes. Ten Thousand Thieves of Life and Honor. Did you know I forged that weapon when the world was young? I spent nearly a century seeking out the most wicked thieves in all of Heaven and Earth, those whose thefts and lies brought an end to loved ones, to cities, to empires. For ten years did I stand at the heart of Black Volcano, smelting those souls down that they might become the base for my greatest weapon. And now you say you seek a new sword? Pray tell, what mistake did I make when I created this one?&quot;<br /> <br /> Unending Darkness' gaze slowly slipped to the ground where it remained. He let out a small sigh and then looked up into the frozen rictus-mask of his master. &quot;It... it screams at me, my lord.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask didn't move for several moments. &quot;It... pardon, what? It screams?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes,&quot; Unending Darkness stated. &quot;It <b>screams</b> at me,&quot; he repeated, emphasizing the word. &quot;Honestly, it's rather aggravating. So, if it's not too troublesome, could I perhaps get a different sword?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It screams?&quot; The Mask said, seemingly incredulous. &quot;Well of course it bloody well screams. It's made out of ten thousand souls trapped in eternal torment after all. I mean, I'd certainly be screaming if that happened to me.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it might sound obvious, but I'll have you know, I haven't had a good nights rest in months. Every time I try to fall asleep, this thing,&quot; he said, shaking the sheathed sword, &quot;starts screaming at me. And that lack of sleep is starting to make me rather cross.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters seemed to be searching for something and then finally asked, &quot;Well, have you maybe tried telling it to stop screaming?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course!&quot; Unending Darkness responded, exasperated. &quot;But when I tell it to stop screaming, that just makes it scream at me even more! I understand ten thousand souls trapped in eternal torment wouldn't exactly be happy, but even still I think it has a very terrible attitude for a sword. I mean...&quot;<br /> <br /> He stopped speaking for a moment and the Mask of Winters urged him on. &quot;Yes...?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, like last week, for instance. I was trying to sneak into the palace of the Walker in Darkness. I was thinking that maybe I could find some dirt or useful information on him.&quot; He looked up to see the Mask of Winters nodding.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yes, that would certainly make me quite pleased. So what happened?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, in the middle of my sneaking around, this thing,&quot; he shook the sheathed sword again, &quot;started screaming for no reason. It blew my cover and I ended up getting my arm chopped off. I mean, yes, Seven-Degrees Physician put a new one me later, but I swear this sword was laughing at me the whole time.&quot;<br /> <br /> As if to confirm it, the sword made a moan that really did sound rather like laughter if you cocked your ear just right.<br /> <br /> &quot;See? Really, I think it hates me.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, nonsense,&quot; The Mask of Winters said soothingly. &quot;I mean, of course it hates you, but it hates everyone. And even if it does prove to be a slight bother when your sneaking around, you have to admit, it is a very good sword. I spent ten years making it after all.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well it certainly is good if you ignore the screaming but even then, that's not the only problem...&quot; Unending Darkness paused and looked around at the gallery of ghosts, all of whom were doing their best to pretend they weren't listening. He sighed and then leaned in closer and whispered, &quot;The truth is, I haven't been able to have sex with my wife in almost three months.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters was glad that his facial features were obscured by his mask. &quot;Y-you don't say.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unending Darkness continued, &quot;Every time my wife and I start, well you know, doing anything, this sword starts moaning like it's trying to join in. At first we thought it was a little amusing, but now it just completely ruins the mood. It's definitely doing it on purpose.&quot; He roughly shook the sword again for good measure.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters sat, silent and still as a statue.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know, last night I chucked it off the side of the Juggernaut.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Y-you chucked Ten Thousand Thieves of Life and Honor, one of my finest creations off the Juggernaut? I spent ten years forging it!&quot; The Mask of Winters was shocked.<br /> <br /> &quot;And then,&quot; Unending Darkness stubbornly continued, &quot;I immediately went to my quarters and started engaging in affairs with my wife. But wouldn't you know it, not even five minutes later this thing,&quot; he shook the sword again as it suddenly began making lascivious moans, &quot;suddenly popped back into my room, screaming and moaning worse than ever. The Maiden of the Mirthless Smile came and knocked on our door and told us to keep it down. It was quite embarrassing for everyone.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, oh yes. I remember I enchanted it so it would always return to its owner when lost,&quot; the Mask mumbled. &quot;Well...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Can't I <b>please</b> get a new sword?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winter sighed and slowly stood up. &quot;Alright, alright. Come back here.&quot; He walked behind his massive throne and there was a series of crates and barrels. Out of one of them poked the handles of a half-dozen different daiklaves. The Mask of Winters reached down and grabbed one seemingly at random.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is Enshadowed by the Darkness, forged from jade which has never seen the light of the Unconquered Sun and combined wi-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Does it scream?&quot; Unending Darkness suddenly interrupted.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wha-? Umm, not that I'm aware of,&quot; the Mask of Winters responded.<br /> <br /> &quot;Does it make moaning sounds?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't believe so.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Will I finally be able to have sex with my wife while that sword is in the room?&quot;<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters, obviously flustered, flailed his arms up and down. &quot;Like, I guess?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Good, I'll take it.&quot; Unending Darkness reached out and grabbed the jade daiklave while placing Ten Thousand Thieves of Life and Honor in the Mask of Winters hands. Then he turned and quickly stomped out of the throne room.<br /> <br /> The Mask of Winters stood there and stared down at the sword in his hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;Urr hurr hurr,&quot; it moaned. It definitely sounded like it was laughing.<br /> <br /> The ancient and feared Deathlord sighed and then walked out from behind his throne. He slowly looked around at the countless ghosts and advisors. &quot;Umm,&quot; he started to speak. Every eye in the place locked onto him immediately.<br /> <br /> &quot;Any murder-hobos here interested in a slightly used daiklave? I guess I should let you know beforehand, it screams. I did spend 10 years making it though.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T13:42:00-07:00","id":912413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912405#post912405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suspect with the new rules you're more likely to see Deathknights branching out and using other magical items than the reverse (and for very good reason, screaming swords have their drawbacks.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont know how yet but I will be damned if I dont find a way to include a Deathknight being slowly driven to madness (of the annoyance variety) by his Soulsteel weapon now...<br /> Well done good sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:03:07-07:00","id":912423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912405#post912405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Any murder-hobos here interested in a slightly used daiklave? &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/14xFtRMKKza7WU/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The entire damn thing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:09:38-07:00","id":912425,"title":"","content":"Something I'll note about the 5-dot soulsteel Artifact we have in the core that was made by a Solar and was wielded by them and some Dragon Blooded is that it comes across as a fairly palatable example of the thing. I mean, it's powered by the souls of murderers and is used to punish the wicked. <br /> <br /> \u200bI feel as though references to soulsteel being rarely used in the First Age was a matter of it being difficult for many Exalted to develop Artifacts that would have characteristics that they would be happy with; I could look on Black Wind as being a bit of a stretch to apply the powers natural to that material to a purpose that would be suitable for those kinds of heroes.<br /> <br /> So I think Abyssals can naturally get more out of soulsteel if one imagines them as vastly more likely to explore its possibilities.<br /> <br /> That and I feel that Volcano Cutter sets a strong precedent for the most powerful Artifact weapons often requiring associated manses to power them, especially their greatest Evocations, and I'd say that most of the good Abyssal manses in the Underworld have fallen under the power of the Deathlords.<br /> <br /> I think for Evocations to give Artifacts some character is a much stronger way of distinguishing them and marking their associations then there ever was before. Hell, it might be stronger than bonestriders and necrotech; I'm pretty sure that Solars could cast those spells.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:18:40-07:00","id":912646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912082#post912082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't even need to make necromancy its own thing, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except if Necromancy is just a different initation into otherwise mechanically identical Sorcery, without a separate spell-list then Solars and Abyssals are equally good at both Sorcery and Necromancy, which would be nonsensical IMO. Solars and Infernals should be <i><b>the</b></i> masters of Sorcery. Abyssals should be <b><i>unequaled</i></b> masters of Necromancy. Lunars and Sidereals should be unable to initiate past the first circle, while most Terrestrials and Infernals should have at least severe difficulty using it, if they can at all. That doesn't work if all spellcasting is the same, just with slightly different window-dressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-12-2016, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T22:38:28-07:00","id":912650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912646#post912646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except if Necromancy is just a different initation into otherwise mechanically identical Sorcery, without a separate spell-list then Solars and Abyssals are equally good at both Sorcery and Necromancy, which would be nonsensical IMO. Solars and Infernals should be <i><b>the</b></i> masters of Sorcery. Abyssals should be <b><i>unequaled</i></b> masters of Necromancy. Lunars and Sidereals should be unable to initiate past the first circle, while most Terrestrials and Infernals should have at least severe difficulty using it, if they can at all. That doesn't work if all spellcasting is the same, just with slightly different window-dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's how I'm guessing it'll work. <br /> <br /> Necromancy spells will have their own tag - Necromancy. They'll be split up into 3 spells and be right there alongside Sorcery. If you have a Necromancy Initiation, you'll be able to learn the highest level of spells you would normally be able to learn, but only if they have the Necromancy tag. At the same time, you wouldn't be able to cast spells of that highest level that <i>don't</i> have the Necromancy tag. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you would be able to cast all spells from lower Circles, regardless of whether they have the Necromancy tag or not. <br /> <br /> So, for example, take two Lunars. One has a Necromancy Initiation, the other has a Sorcery Initiation. Both have access to Second Circle Sorcery. <br /> <br /> The first Lunar, the Necromancer, can cast any Terrestrial level spell, regardless of whether it has the Necromancy tag or not. However, for Second Circle spells, he can <i>only</i> cast spells with the Necromancy tag. Meanwhile, the second Lunar can cast any spell of the Terrestrial Circle, regardless of its tags, but he can only cast spells that <i>don't</i> have the Necromancy tag. <br /> <br /> This means that you still make a choice, whether to focus on Necromancy or Sorcery, but it doesn't make Necromancy it's own style of not-Sorcery, and anybody can learn a few lower end Necromancy spells without having to dedicate themselves and picking up special Charms (Shadowland Circle Necromancy, Labyrinth Circle, Void Circle, as was the case in 1st and 2nd edition). <br /> <br /> This does run into the fact that it would be possible to have a Solar or Infernal capable of learning Third Circle Necromancy spells (if they have a Necromancy Intitiation) and likewise Abyssals could cast Solar Circle Sorcery (if they had a Sorcery Initiation), but I don't really see that as a huge issue. I don't think the setting is going to fall apart if there isn't hard-coded niche protection. Just because there was in prior editions doesn't make it the &quot;best way&quot; or necessary, though I'm open for reasons why it should remain in Third Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T05:23:27-07:00","id":912747,"title":"","content":"I've noticed that allowing non-Abyssal Necromancers to go further into Necromancy is a really common house rule.<br /> Black Ice Shadow types are regularly told &quot;fuck it you can learn Labyrinth instead of Celestial&quot; and on a splatwide level, fanworks like Terrifying Argent Witches made Lunars equally adept at both Sorcery and Necromancy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T07:54:33-07:00","id":912797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912646#post912646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except if Necromancy is just a different initation into otherwise mechanically identical Sorcery, without a separate spell-list then Solars and Abyssals are equally good at both Sorcery and Necromancy, which would be nonsensical IMO. Solars and Infernals should be <i><b>the</b></i> masters of Sorcery. Abyssals should be <b><i>unequaled</i></b> masters of Necromancy. Lunars and Sidereals should be unable to initiate past the first circle, while most Terrestrials and Infernals should have at least severe difficulty using it, if they can at all. That doesn't work if all spellcasting is the same, just with slightly different window-dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shaping rituals went a long way toward making sorcery cool, weird, and distinct, so shaping rituals can probably also make the difference more ably for necromancy and infernal sorcery. We already have pieces of the latter case, in the form of learning sorcery from Mara, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T08:45:25-07:00","id":912821,"title":"","content":"Erinys doesn't actually have Ex3 yet, so she probably doesn't know about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T08:53:08-07:00","id":912825,"title":"","content":"Robert Vance already did say that Necromancy will be different when somebody asked about the Nephwrack QC using regular sorcery(just because Necromancy system wasn't finished at the time), as in not just a different shaping ritual , so the spells list are definitely going to be separated again and so are the circles. On top of it, with them going with the idea that the Abyssals are dropping the mirror charms and the likes...wouldn't be surprised if it is even more difficult to do necromancy for non abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T13:05:50-07:00","id":912960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltacolibre</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912825#post912825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of it, with them going with the idea that the Abyssals are dropping the mirror charms and the likes...wouldn't be surprised if it is even more difficult to do necromancy for non abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't bet on that. My experience is that non Abyssal Necromancers are a popular PC niche and Abyssal players express sentiments that Necromancy stole a huge chunk of death themed magic away from their native charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T14:57:56-07:00","id":913015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911928#post911928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>My</i> reaction would be &quot;dogs don't behave like that. They don't bite 'out of nowhere.' Either that animal has been abused in a way that causes it to attack based off a trigger that's otherwise innocuous, or it's been TRAINED to attack off a trigger that's otherwise innocuous. What the fuck have you been doing to that poor animal?&quot;<br /> <br /> Some other people might take you at your word, though, because they're ignorant of dogs and how they behave. That doesn't make them wrong. That just means they trusted you when they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Plenty of people are going to totally buy the Immaculate line on the Anathema. But some people are not. Because they don't trust the Immaculate Order. Because they think &quot;well that's a mighty fine catch-22 you've constructed with regard to the Anathema, isn't it? REAL fine, that catch-22. Especially the part where you demand we give you all our jade to protect us from them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great way to answer the question without actually addressing the point. Regarding the Anathema, you have one expert: the Immaculate Order. You work with an Anathema, trust an Anathema, you are risking your life and soul. Peasants in Creation haven't the time to conceive of &quot;Catch 22&quot; or &quot;propaganda.&quot; They aren't educated or raised to be skeptical. They see death and instability every day, their only protection from rogue gods and bandits is the Realm, and you're talking as if they are hipster urban elites with macbooks and a six-figure education.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can run Creation that way, but that Creation can't support the Realm's hegemony, and it makes Celestials' challenge level drop significantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:03:41-07:00","id":913019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913015#post913015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a great way to answer the question without actually addressing the point. Regarding the Anathema, you have one expert: <b>the Immaculate Order</b>. You work with an Anathema, trust an Anathema, you are risking your life and soul. Peasants in Creation haven't the time to conceive of &quot;Catch 22&quot; or &quot;propaganda.&quot; They aren't educated or raised to be skeptical. They see death and instability every day, their only protection from rogue gods and bandits is the Realm, and you're talking as if they are hipster urban elites with macbooks and a six-figure education.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can run Creation that way, but that Creation can't support the Realm's hegemony, and it makes Celestials' challenge level drop significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Philosophy. The Immaculate Philosophy. The Immaculate Order is the Realm's branch, but it concurs with Lookshy's branch and likely that of the Forest Witches regarding most of the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:23:27-07:00","id":913025,"title":"","content":"I think critical thinking about catch-22s isn't relevant to how most people thing. But, the Realm is extremely oppressive, and some Anathema offer an alternative. Some people will buy into the lies that make that oppression &quot;legitimate&quot; because people do in real life too. But some people will look around and ask why it's better to have your children raped or sold as slaves by the Dynasts, than cutting a deal with a corrupt god or following an Anathema native to your own society who wants to free the kingdom.<br /> <br /> In any place where Realm hegemony is a matter of a foreign army occupying land that they conquered, or even stole by forcing the natives off the land/ethnic cleansing/enslaving the entire population, the Immaculates have to compete with the native beliefs and the desire of every human being to survive and be free from slavery, see their kids survive and be free, and believe their life has value.<br /> <br /> When you brutalize somebody so thoroughly that they have nothing left to lose, they will usually be willing to accept nearly any alternative they can find. Anathema, Yozi cults, corrupt gods, ancestor cults, Deathlord religions, whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-12-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T18:59:30-07:00","id":913147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=912960#post912960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't bet on that. My experience is that non Abyssal Necromancers are a popular PC niche and Abyssal players express sentiments that Necromancy stole a huge chunk of death themed magic away from their native charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe I'm alone here, but I'd prefer LESS death focus in the Abyssal charmset. But that might be just because the specter of 2e where most Abyssal charms were just &quot;Like the Solar, but less good/only able to do death stuff.&quot; It made Abyssals feel like bad attempted copies of Solars.<br /> <br /> Now I'm imagining the Deathlords all have Exaltation copy machines, but not enough toner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:05:57-07:00","id":913152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913015#post913015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a great way to answer the question without actually addressing the point. Regarding the Anathema, you have one expert: the Immaculate Order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people are going to hate and loathe the Immaculate Order and the philosophy they espouse, because the Immaculate Order is a boot on the back of their necks. Those people are going to view with skepticism anything it says.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't educated or raised to be skeptical. They see death and instability every day, their only protection from rogue gods and bandits is the Realm, and you're talking as if they are hipster urban elites with macbooks and a six-figure education. </div> </div> </div>Just because people aren't educated doesn't mean they're not <i>smart</i>.<br /> <br /> But even that notwithstanding, people who see the Realm as their only protection from rogue gods and bandits will, indeed, be willing to take the Immaculate Order at its word when it comes to the Anathema.<br /> <br /> There are going to be lots of people who don't see the Realm as their only protection. There are, in fact, going to be a lot of people who view the Realm as a vile oppressor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:13:15-07:00","id":913159,"title":"","content":"But...pardon I seem to have lost track. Lookshy is wholly independent of the realm, has basically the same immaculate philosphy with regards to anathema, and prides itself as inheritor of the shogunate. People in and outside the realm might be more lenient, but with regards to Lookshy, they seem perfectly against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T19:50:58-07:00","id":913172,"title":"","content":"Yeah any Solar who advertises their presence to Lookshy is going to get a Wyld Hunt in response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T20:11:44-07:00","id":913181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913159#post913159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But...pardon I seem to have lost track. Lookshy is wholly independent of the realm, has basically the same immaculate philosphy with regards to anathema, and prides itself as inheritor of the shogunate. People in and outside the realm might be more lenient, but with regards to Lookshy, they seem perfectly against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, absolutely. Lookshyans aren't going to be fans of Solars.<br /> <br /> The thing is, though, while the Immaculate Philosophy is part of Lookshy's state apparatus, they haven't weaponized it and begun using it as a tool of imperial oppression and cultural control in quite the same way the Realm has. <i>And</i> the fact that they aren't a global hegemon means they have to be practical. They can't march into Great Forks and force the gods there to act properly. They can't march into Nexus and root out the known Anathema who base out of there. Indeed, they had to tolerate an Abyssal Exalted as the official representative of his polity to the Confederation of Rivers and accord him honor as a diplomat. Covert Wyld Hunts are a possibility, but when a bunch of organized Dragon-Blooded do some murders in your neck of the woods, you're going to suspiciously turn your gaze towards Lookshy.<br /> <br /> But the upshot is that Lookshy is already used to tolerating the Anathema when it has to, which means if shit gets real they're probably going to be way more willing to extend a cautious hand than others would be, as I brought up previously in the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T20:23:08-07:00","id":913185,"title":"","content":"If the Mask of Winters is marching on Lookshy, and Karal Fire Orchid shows up at the Gens Karal residence saying she wants to help... I give even odds on Linwei coming back from the General Staff with notice they'll look the other way until the current emergency is over, or with a Wyld Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T21:04:53-07:00","id":913210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913181#post913181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, absolutely. Lookshyans aren't going to be fans of Solars.<br /> <br /> The thing is, though, while the Immaculate Philosophy is part of Lookshy's state apparatus, they haven't weaponized it and begun using it as a tool of imperial oppression and cultural control in quite the same way the Realm has. <i>And</i> the fact that they aren't a global hegemon means they have to be practical. They can't march into Great Forks and force the gods there to act properly. They can't march into Nexus and root out the known Anathema who base out of there. Indeed, they had to tolerate an Abyssal Exalted as the official representative of his polity to the Confederation of Rivers and accord him honor as a diplomat. Covert Wyld Hunts are a possibility, but when a bunch of organized Dragon-Blooded do some murders in your neck of the woods, you're going to suspiciously turn your gaze towards Lookshy.<br /> <br /> But the upshot is that Lookshy is already used to tolerating the Anathema when it has to, which means if shit gets real they're probably going to be way more willing to extend a cautious hand than others would be, as I brought up previously in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is generally what I am hoping that they do with Lookshy, I can accept their new found Zealotry (it takes a certain amount of it to devout your life to a religious endevour with few tangible rewards and incredible risk) as long as it is a more informal event. As long as they are altogether willing to tolerate a seemingly 'harmless' Anathema over being curbstomped by a more tangible threat then they still retain the pragmatism that I always liked about the city-state.<br /> <br /> Although as I say that I find myself hoping that they explore other cities in Lookshian territory this edition. They have previously mentioned several minor towns but it was not uncommon for Italian city-states to have lesser cities under their control and they held comparitably little land when comparing Italy (&amp; Vencian territory beyond it) to the vast swaths of territory within the Scavenger Lands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:13:56-07:00","id":913238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913181#post913181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, absolutely. Lookshyans aren't going to be fans of Solars.<br /> <br /> The thing is, though, while the Immaculate Philosophy is part of Lookshy's state apparatus, they haven't weaponized it and begun using it as a tool of imperial oppression and cultural control in quite the same way the Realm has. <i>And</i> the fact that they aren't a global hegemon means they have to be practical. They can't march into Great Forks and force the gods there to act properly. They can't march into Nexus and root out the known Anathema who base out of there. <b>Indeed, they had to tolerate an Abyssal Exalted as the official representative of his polity to the Confederation of Rivers and accord him honor as a diplomat.</b> Covert Wyld Hunts are a possibility, but when a bunch of organized Dragon-Blooded do some murders in your neck of the woods, you're going to suspiciously turn your gaze towards Lookshy.<br /> <br /> But the upshot is that Lookshy is already used to tolerating the Anathema when it has to, which means if shit gets real they're probably going to be way more willing to extend a cautious hand than others would be, as I brought up previously in the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely not in EX3, since the Mask isn't interested in talking things out. Typhon, the Wink of the Storm's Eye, is probably going to go back to his 1e core presentation of being an actual spy, presenting himself as a wandering mercenary. At least, until he uses Incomparable Body Arsenal. Oddly enough, if you keep his Essence at the same value it was back then, he can actually use Celestial Circle spells in the new edition!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:36:20-07:00","id":913243,"title":"","content":"I imagine that Lookshy is generally going to find it a bit difficult to send Wyld Hunts into other nations, depending on the circumstances, and they likely won't bother if an Anathema doesn't particularly draw their attention. So even if word reaches Lookshy of some Anathema working as a detective in Nexus, they probably aren't going to round up a team of badass warriors to go after them. Such warriors are irreplaceable and not worth going after random Anathema who aren't causing any real threat.<br /> <br /> If, however, they hear about an Anathema who is a threat, like a Dawn Caste uniting the Hundred Kingdoms, that would absolutely draw a Wyld Hunt. Essentially, the moment a Solar poses some sort of threat (real or imagined) to Lookshy's hegemony or base of power, they will be facing a Wyld Hunt. <br /> <br /> So for Exalted who keep their heads down and don't draw undo attention to themselves, they won't have to worry about an <b>official</b> Lookshyan Wyld Hunt. <br /> <br /> That said, the local Dragon Blooded near where the Solar is active might decide to get a Wyld Hunt together to kill the Anathema. They do that a lot. And they would absolutely be able to recruit any Lookshayan Dragon Blooded who are stationed nearby to join them. In fact, those local Lookshayn soldiers might take it under their own initiative to go kill the Anathema if they find out one is nearby and then send word back to Lookshy, depending on their own personal views of Anathema.<br /> <br /> So while an official Lookshyan Wyld Hunt might not come after a Solar in the Scavenger Lands, an ad-hoc Wyld Hunt is always a real possibility, and with Lookshayan soldiers stationed around the Scavenger Lands, could very well see &quot;unofficial&quot; Lookshyan Wyld Hunts coming after Anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:48:30-07:00","id":913244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913238#post913238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typhon, the Wink of the Storm's Eye</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick aside question: How does this Abyssal have a name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:53:46-07:00","id":913246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913244#post913244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick aside question: How does this Abyssal have a name?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's probably not his real name, just a short-hand name he uses, probably due to the fact that it's easier to just sign &quot;Typhon&quot; than &quot;The Wink of the Storm's Eye,&quot; when filling out paperwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:03:12-07:00","id":913255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913246#post913246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's probably not his real name, just a short-hand name he uses, probably due to the fact that it's easier to just sign &quot;Typhon&quot; than &quot;The Wink of the Storm's Eye,&quot; when filling out paperwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always joke that most Deathlords dont actually bother to keep their Abyssal names in writing and just use acronyms for most of the paperwork. Unless you are the Bishop of course since I guess it aids his everlasting quest to add to his word count...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:29:36-07:00","id":913264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913244#post913244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick aside question: How does this Abyssal have a name?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was presumably created in a slightly earlier iteration of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:11:50-07:00","id":913274,"title":"","content":"It's not that Abyssals <i>must</i> go by <i>no</i> name, it's that they can't go by their <i>living</i> name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:26:55-07:00","id":913282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911210#post911210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is quickly becoming a reservation of mine when dealing with 3rd (even though it has done a marvelous job of convincing me until now), I feel like it makes Lookshy and the Realm too similar, I always thought that Lookshy had a very Shinto approach to their faith with it being very secondary to their ancient Greek style Nationalism. It really does just feel painfully unnecessary to have yet another group devouted to ending Solars. It should honestly at least occur to at least some Lookshyians that a Solar could be Lookshyian first and Anathema second.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's good to see that the Immaculate ideology can exist in different forms. Lookshy's entire identity, first and foremost, is being the direct continuation of the Shogunate. As in the Shogunate that was formed out of the Usurpation and created the Wyld Hunt in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now as has been said, there is more room for &quot;hard men of hard decisions&quot; military pragmatism on the part of the 7th Legion, as military concerns trump everything, unlike with the Realm's Wyld Hunt which is completely operated by the Immaculate Order as it's own entity separate from the Legions. BUT, that same &quot;pragmatism&quot; is going to make them skeptical at best of a being as powerful as a Solar not being a threat to their cultivated balance of power in the River Province.<br /> <br /> Even a &quot;Solar Lookshyian&quot;, is going to be actively seen as a threatening to the existing authorities, even without Immaculate ideology being in-play! How can they maintain their authority with this God-King around!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-13-2016, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T00:52:37-07:00","id":913290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913282#post913282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's good to see that the Immaculate ideology can exist in different forms. Lookshy's entire identity, first and foremost, is being the direct continuation of the Shogunate. As in the Shogunate that was formed out of the Usurpation and created the Wyld Hunt in the first place.<br /> <br /> Now as has been said, there is more room for &quot;hard men of hard decisions&quot; military pragmatism on the part of the 7th Legion, as military concerns trump everything, unlike with the Realm's Wyld Hunt which is completely operated by the Immaculate Order as it's own entity separate from the Legions. BUT, that same &quot;pragmatism&quot; is going to make the skeptical at best to a being as powerful as a Solar not being a threat to their cultivated balance of power in the River Province.<br /> <br /> Even a &quot;Solar Lookshyian&quot;, is going to be actively seen as a threat being the existing authorities, even without Immaculate ideology being in-play! How can they maintain their authority with this God-King around!</div> </div> </div> </div>And any Lookshyian who becomes a Solar is probably A) going to want to be elsewhere and B) is not unlikely to be either a current or former military badass who knows their mood well enough to realize it's probably not a bad time to look for somewhere else to live. Even if you're loyal to Lookshy, you're probably going to try and help them without being obvious about it. Those Solars are just as likely as commanders to be pragmatic and realize little good comes from sticking around.<br /> <br /> That said, I could totally see other Solars being arrogant or naive enough to believe Lookshy was just looking for reasons to really be friends (or could be easily subverted, whatever they want). And those are the ones who get themselves killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T07:52:41-07:00","id":913379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913274#post913274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that Abyssals <i>must</i> go by <i>no</i> name, it's that they can't go by their <i>living</i> name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typhon was implied to be his living name, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T08:14:35-07:00","id":913387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=911229#post911229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even back in earliest 1e, in <i>Castebook: Zenith</i>, the Lookshy General Staff were getting ready to hunt down and kill their own decorated, honored veteran, and daughter of one of their own membership, Karal Fire Orchid, for Exalting as a Solar. You'd think that if they had ever had enough pragmatism to work with a Solar, &quot;The one who's a loyal Lookshyan soldier and the daughter of one of our general staff, who Exalted protecting a village from a Fair Folk raid&quot; would be the one they'd be like &quot;Sure, she doesn't sound so bad&quot; about.<br /> <br /> But no. Anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why this was cited as a reason why Lookshy would be particularly unreasonable...<br /> <br /> Look, picture it this way.<br /> <br /> If the United States were involved in some sort of serious middle east conflict with extremists, and some great glowing demigod popped up that might help us with that conflict, we might be reasonably inclined to try to harness that power to defeat our enemy. We must remember that in this example, the 'United States' has dealt with ALL SORTS of horrible spirits, elementals and demons previously - and; has a negotiated PEACE with a Deathlord.<br /> <br /> Now, let's take that situation and tweak it slightly! A major GENERAL has become the glowing demigod! And, she's back in Washington! In fact, she's like... the Secretary of Defense's daughter!<br /> <br /> Is this LESS or MORE threatening to the President (General Staff)?<br /> <br /> The answer is obviously more - Karal Fire Orchid ABSOLUTELY needs to be destroyed, but the fact that the General Staff came down on her so hard should certainly not be taken as evidence of a zealous need to destroy Anathema. No, that's pure ruthless pragmatism, right there. Of COURSE when a major General, with a huge victory and vast sympathy from the troops, develops this power it's a big deal. She became a huge threat to the establishment right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> That kind of an issue needs to be dealt with immediately. But if you have an Anathema in a relatively distant theater, who is one among a horde of enemies that all want to kill each other? Go nuts, throw a few treaties together, we can just break them later anyway.<br /> <br /> This is how I personally think Lookshy would have viewed that situation, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 06-13-2016, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:05:51-07:00","id":913562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913290#post913290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And any Lookshyian who becomes a Solar is probably A) going to want to be elsewhere and B) is not unlikely to be either a current or former military badass who knows their mood well enough to realize it's probably not a bad time to look for somewhere else to live. Even if you're loyal to Lookshy, you're probably going to try and help them without being obvious about it. Those Solars are just as likely as commanders to be pragmatic and realize little good comes from sticking around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a guy playing a Lookshyian Twilight...<br /> <br /> Yeah, you pretty much hit it on the nose. Well okay, he was a mortal on track to become a Sorcerer-Engineer rather than a hardened captain, but still... When he Exalted, he ran like hell and vanished for a few years. And he only dared go back to Lookshy after using the Last Supplicant/Penitent of the Lap to basically strike a blow against the undead army attacking Lookshy, in addition to setting it up to actively move to counteract all Shadowlands in Creation.<br /> <br /> Even then, his welcome was... <i>Tentative</i>. There's still members of the Staff who'd sooner kill him and be done with it. The understanding is that he mostly stay outside Lookshy itself, assisting them that way, and if he DOES return to Lookshy, don't stay longer than a couple of days, and do NOT start glowing, because if he's publicly outed as a Solar his head will be on a pike faster than you can say &quot;Plausible Deniability&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:43:03-07:00","id":913587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913562#post913562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking as a guy playing a Lookshyian Twilight...<br /> <br /> Yeah, you pretty much hit it on the nose. Well okay, he was a mortal on track to become a Sorcerer-Engineer rather than a hardened captain, but still... When he Exalted, he ran like hell and vanished for a few years. And he only dared go back to Lookshy after using the Last Supplicant/Penitent of the Lap to basically strike a blow against the undead army attacking Lookshy, in addition to setting it up to actively move to counteract all Shadowlands in Creation.<br /> <br /> Even then, his welcome was... <i>Tentative</i>. There's still members of the Staff who'd sooner kill him and be done with it. The understanding is that he mostly stay outside Lookshy itself, assisting them that way, and if he DOES return to Lookshy, don't stay longer than a couple of days, and do NOT start glowing, because if he's publicly outed as a Solar his head will be on a pike faster than you can say &quot;Plausible Deniability&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My Lookshyian Twilight also ran after her Exaltation.<br /> <br /> But, I want Lookshy to be something different than &quot;Another Dragonblooded culture that kills Solars, no questions asked.&quot; I don't want them to be throwing a party when one of their Sorcerer Engineer's exalts as a Twilight, but some pragmatic hypocrisy wouldn't be out of place. The General Staff could be &quot;Yeah, I'd like to stick a Jade Diaklaive in his back, but that Anathema is just too damn useful.&quot; And as soon as the Solar isn't useful. WHACK! <br /> <br /> I'm not talking about a happy fun situation for the Solar here, just something different than what the Realm &quot;offers&quot; Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:48:05-07:00","id":913595,"title":"","content":"I mostly want Lookshy to feel less monolithic. It's got multiple Dragon-Blooded Gentes with their own political interests there's not an empty throne to highlight this as much as there is with the Realm but presumably there are interesting things that can be done with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T12:50:33-07:00","id":913600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913595#post913595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly want Lookshy to feel less monolithic. It's got multiple Dragon-Blooded Gentes with their own political interests there's not an empty throne to highlight this as much as there is with the Realm but presumably there are interesting things that can be done with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I assume there's a political divide between the more forward thinking sorcerer crafter types and the more conservative military officers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:00:30-07:00","id":913607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913595#post913595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly want Lookshy to feel less monolithic. It's got multiple Dragon-Blooded Gentes with their own political interests there's not an empty throne to highlight this as much as there is with the Realm but presumably there are interesting things that can be done with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with this.<br /> <br /> One angle I think needs to be considered is that Lookshy DBs arent quite as cloistered off from the rest of the world as those in the Realm. While the general populace may want to lynch you and the General Staff may consider using you from a safe (political) distance with a daiklave to your neck, the DB that you have served under for the last decade who you went through boot camp with is probably going to be more willing to hear you out.<br /> In the Realm on the other hand all of your friends are DBs and if a relative exalts then you are probably even less likely to spare her than if she were a random villager.<br /> It is that dichotomy in behaviour and worldview that I want to see explored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T13:40:58-07:00","id":913630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913595#post913595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly want Lookshy to feel less monolithic. It's got multiple Dragon-Blooded Gentes with their own political interests there's not an empty throne to highlight this as much as there is with the Realm but presumably there are interesting things that can be done with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. My Twilight WAS basically used by different factions of the Staff. As mentioned, many wanted him dead, but surprisingly, Karal Linwei spoke up in his defense.<br /> <br /> It was all a ploy, but seeing an Anathema who was still a loyal Lookshyan gave her hope that maybe, just maybe, her daughter was still her daughter. My Twilight didn't object to being used to push an agenda because it meant he got to visit his home again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T15:57:51-07:00","id":913700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913387#post913387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure why this was cited as a reason why Lookshy would be particularly unreasonable...<br /> <br /> Look, picture it this way.<br /> <br /> If the United States were involved in some sort of serious middle east conflict with extremists, and some great glowing demigod popped up that might help us with that conflict, we might be reasonably inclined to try to harness that power to defeat our enemy. We must remember that in this example, the 'United States' has dealt with ALL SORTS of horrible spirits, elementals and demons previously - and; has a negotiated PEACE with a Deathlord.<br /> <br /> Now, let's take that situation and tweak it slightly! A major GENERAL has become the glowing demigod! And, she's back in Washington! In fact, she's like... the Secretary of Defense's daughter!<br /> <br /> Is this LESS or MORE threatening to the President (General Staff)?<br /> <br /> The answer is obviously more - Karal Fire Orchid ABSOLUTELY needs to be destroyed, but the fact that the General Staff came down on her so hard should certainly not be taken as evidence of a zealous need to destroy Anathema. No, that's pure ruthless pragmatism, right there. Of COURSE when a major General, with a huge victory and vast sympathy from the troops, develops this power it's a big deal. She became a huge threat to the establishment right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> That kind of an issue needs to be dealt with immediately. But if you have an Anathema in a relatively distant theater, who is one among a horde of enemies that all want to kill each other? Go nuts, throw a few treaties together, we can just break them later anyway.<br /> <br /> This is how I personally think Lookshy would have viewed that situation, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some breakdowns in your analogy. Fire Orchid was retired, and she made it only as far as mortals are allowed in the ranks (Kazei, the equivalent of an Army/Air Force Colonel or Navy Captain, and one rank below a Brigadier (one-star) General or lower-grade Rear Admiral) before she called it quits. She had no active troops, but was basically just doing what US policy kind of did through the 80s: training lots of scattered people in warfare to repel a mutual threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:34:43-07:00","id":913720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913587#post913587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My Lookshyian Twilight also ran after her Exaltation.<br /> <br /> But, I want Lookshy to be something different than &quot;Another Dragonblooded culture that kills Solars, no questions asked.&quot; I don't want them to be throwing a party when one of their Sorcerer Engineer's exalts as a Twilight, but some pragmatic hypocrisy wouldn't be out of place. The General Staff could be &quot;Yeah, I'd like to stick a Jade Diaklaive in his back, but that Anathema is just too damn useful.&quot; And as soon as the Solar isn't useful. WHACK!<br /> <br /> I'm not talking about a happy fun situation for the Solar here, just something different than what the Realm &quot;offers&quot; Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is how you take the &quot;The enemy of my enemy is my friend&quot; stuff. It's an old adage, but there's a lot of ink written on how that is actually tactically a disaster long term and simply sets yourself up for failure. If it is a situation you could have handled without Anathema, you don't use Anathema. if it is a situation you can't handle without Anathema, don't get in that situation in the first fucking place, is the more sound real world pragmatist option.<br /> <br /> Because it's worth remembering that the Immaculate hitlist on Anathema isn't just becuase of demons: It's because at its core the Philosophy is about Terrestrial Hegemony and Anathema of any stripe threaten this. Lookshy being hostile to Solars doesn't necessarily even mean it's going to be the same, either. For Lookshy, it might just be more nakedly political than with the Realm, for instance. Not all conflict is the same, afterall.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T16:47:53-07:00","id":913728,"title":"","content":"In fairness, I too had a Lookshyian Zenith who was a former Gunzosha. Former, because she was done with her period with the armor. Pretty much was a wreck waiting off in a rural village waiting to die (she'd watched all her friends and even her commander die... usually in senseless ways during war). She left and didn't try and do anything with Lookshy. The only time she did was when a nasty behemoth of sorts was fighting DB rangers and it wasn't going great, she convinced the circle to aid them. Because they didn't deserve to die for trying to protect the people of the area.<br /> <br /> On the political thing, at best, I could see Lookshy hiring Solars under the table to do dirty work they don't want to be associated with. Because they're Solars, they're A) expendible B) unexpected to be working for Lookshy and C) they wouldn't expect anything after the mission to go better with Lookshy. Sending two enemies to go murder each other seems efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T18:52:41-07:00","id":913791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913728#post913728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... On the political thing, at best, I could see Lookshy hiring Solars under the table to do dirty work they don't want to be associated with. Because they're Solars, they're A) expendible B) unexpected to be working for Lookshy and C) they wouldn't expect anything after the mission to go better with Lookshy. Sending two enemies to go murder each other seems efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also more interesting a scenario too It hink since if they're found-out or a threat of being found out, you get some cool spy movie cloak-and-daggers hit of whether you're going to get help, convincing them to keep on your side or their betrayal to keep face. You know, plot stuff.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T04:50:27-07:00","id":914012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=913172#post913172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah any Solar who advertises their presence to Lookshy is going to get a Wyld Hunt in response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dawn: &quot;None of you understand. I'm not locked up in here with you. <b>You're locked up in here with me.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T11:52:11-07:00","id":914247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914012#post914012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dawn: &quot;None of you understand. I'm not locked up in here with you. <b>You're locked up in here with me.&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering that Lookshy is probably the only city that has a high enough concentration of DBs to get a Might 3 Battle Group larger than Size 1 together on short notice, and that they will almost certainly have at least average Drill, I am dubious of the Dawn's chances even if she's an ISP. Especially if the DB Battle Group can use Excellencies.<br /> <br /> Can a DB battle Group use Excellencies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T11:58:21-07:00","id":914252,"title":"","content":"One would assume. As can their commander...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T12:27:03-07:00","id":914275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914247#post914247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Considering that Lookshy is probably the only city that has a high enough concentration of DBs to get a Might 3 Battle Group larger than Size 1 together on short notice, and that they will almost certainly have at least average Drill, I am dubious of the Dawn's chances even if she's an ISP. Especially if the DB Battle Group can use Excellencies.<br /> <br /> Can a DB battle Group use Excellencies?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. Their supernatural power is modeled by Might. But they would still be tossing out 30+ die attacks if commanded by a good general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:32:09-07:00","id":914426,"title":"","content":"DBs don't tend to form battle groups, considering a BG relies on the characters in question being similar enough to be relatively interchangeable. <br /> <br /> Also, writer commentary indicates there's nothing stopping battle groups of supernaturals from using Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:35:47-07:00","id":914427,"title":"","content":"When determining how a &quot;pragmatic&quot; NPC might approach Solars, first look at an alternate version of the setting in which the Immaculate Order's views of the Solar and Lunar Exalted <i>are exactly and literally true</i>. If you're playing a Dragon-Blooded PC in that setting and are confronted with a seemingly innocuous, persuasive Anathema who offers assistance... what is the pragmatic approach?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:46:59-07:00","id":914432,"title":"","content":"Could you provide a source? I have not seen anything that indicates that BGs are able to use charms (that seems to be what Might is for). What they could easily do within the rules, is have high magnitude (average of their health levels), and be equipped with artifact gear.<br /> <b>Dragon-Blood</b><br /><br /> Attack:19 Damage:21 Defense:10 Magnitude:12 Soak:15 <br /> <br /> A size 2 group of DBs with good combat stats and artifact gear w/elite drill is tossing out 19 attack dice and 21 damage on every attack, has passive defense of 10 and 15 soak - that is horrifying. A good commander can add 6-8 attack dice with a command action, which is 8-10 with the elite drill bonus, that is 28 attack dice from just a size 2 group!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T15:48:57-07:00","id":914433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914427#post914427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When determining how a &quot;pragmatic&quot; NPC might approach Solars, first look at an alternate version of the setting in which the Immaculate Order's views of the Solar and Lunar Exalted <i>are exactly and literally true</i>. If you're playing a Dragon-Blooded PC in that setting and are confronted with a seemingly innocuous, persuasive Anathema who offers assistance... what is the pragmatic approach?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a case for making a deal with the devil for power. Or for governments sending weapons to terrorist organizations that oppose their enemies. Though, I suppose in Creation you could make a deal with an actual demon instead of an insane sun demon. <br /> <br /> *shrug* At my gaming table, certain individuals in the Seventh Legion will cautiously use Solars. It will probably end in messy betrayal for all parties involved, but hey, that makes good drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:01:04-07:00","id":914504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914432#post914432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you provide a source? I have not seen anything that indicates that BGs are able to use charms (that seems to be what Might is for). What they could easily do within the rules, is have high magnitude (average of their health levels), and be equipped with artifact gear.<br /> <b>Dragon-Blood</b><br /> <br /> Attack:19 Damage:21 Defense:10 Magnitude:12 Soak:15<br /> <br /> A size 2 group of DBs with good combat stats and artifact gear w/elite drill is tossing out 19 attack dice and 21 damage on every attack, has passive defense of 10 and 15 soak - that is horrifying. A good commander can add 6-8 attack dice with a command action, which is 8-10 with the elite drill bonus, that is 28 attack dice from just a size 2 group!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, How did you get the attack dice number? My math says a Size 2 Might 3 Group with the DB Young Dynast QC build has 14 attack dice.<br /> <br /> Edit: Before Excellencies or command actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11917,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","user":"Aranfan","date":". 06-14-2016, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:40:06-07:00","id":914538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you provide a source? I have not seen anything that indicates that BGs are able to use charms </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't they? If they couldn't, a BG of DBs would be far worse than one or two DBs by themselves. DB battle groups ought to be the deadliest battle groups in the game.<br /> <br /> Though presumably they'd only be able to use charms that the whole group (or at least, the vast majority of the group) knows. But certainly excellencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:42:07-07:00","id":914587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914538#post914538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they couldn't, a BG of DBs would be far worse than one or two DBs by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIs that not kind of the point?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:47:46-07:00","id":914592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914587#post914587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIs that not kind of the point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A battle group should be at least stronger than a lone individual of the same stats. Mind, I haven't really played yet, so the inert initiative might suffice, but I do think a DB battlegroup should have access to the excellencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:18:49-07:00","id":914605,"title":"","content":"So, if a BG's Charms are represented by their actual Charms, what is Might doing?<br /> <br /> Also, it makes sense to me that a single, individualized DB should be <i>much </i>better than a battlegroup of DBs. There should only be such a battlegroup in games in which it is acceptable for DBs to be mooks. Elite, but still mooks. Of course an actually-significant-to-the-story DB is gonna be much better.<br /> <br /> I mean, that group of Shaolin monks are all badasses, but the one monk played by Jet Li can still fight a dozen of them at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:24:56-07:00","id":914610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914605#post914605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if a BG's Charms are represented by their actual Charms, what is Might doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Operating as compensation for the lack of force-multipliers like independent charm-fueled actions and mote pools that would be present if the characters involved were functioning individually rather than as a battle-group.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:26:27-07:00","id":914611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914587#post914587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIs that not kind of the point?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be worse than a super-awesome heroic individual. But a bunch of average dudes getting together as a battle group shouldn't be worse than a single average dude.<br /> (This &quot;average&quot; is of course relative, in this case, as &quot;average&quot; for a DB is pretty awesome)<br /> <br /> So, say my Essence 5 PCs attack the local Realm satrapy guarded by a legion, and in the battle there's a unit of 10 young Dragonblood low-ranking officers. Now, it should be worse than the DB general, or his Dragonlords, or his 3 champions who may be low-ranking but are masters of combat, sure. But it shouldn't be worse than 1 young low-ranking DB officer.<br /> <br /> Similarly, a battle group of ninjas isn't going to be as good as a single ninja. But that's because the single ninja is a stand-out Ninja, not just a low-ranking apprentice ninja.<br /> <br /> Also, I agree with Drake about Might.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:37:44-07:00","id":914622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914611#post914611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Similarly, a battle group of ninjas isn't going to be as good as a single ninja. But that's because the single ninja is a stand-out Ninja, not just a low-ranking apprentice ninja.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, this is not a reference to Conservation of Ninjutsu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11867-caffeine-delusions","name":"Caffeine Delusions","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:41:05-07:00","id":914626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914504#post914504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Um, How did you get the attack dice number? My math says a Size 2 Might 3 Group with the DB Young Dynast QC build has 14 attack dice.<br /> <br /> Edit: Before Excellencies or command actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not using a young Dynast QC, a medium artifact wielding DB has a max attack pool of 14 dice. Admittedly, it should be more like 12-13 dice for an &quot;experienced&quot; Dynast. That is still 17-18 dice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:52:58-07:00","id":914637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914538#post914538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't they? If they couldn't, a BG of DBs would be far worse than one or two DBs by themselves. DB battle groups ought to be the deadliest battle groups in the game.<br /> <br /> Though presumably they'd only be able to use charms that the whole group (or at least, the vast majority of the group) knows. But certainly excellencies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't agree with this at all, Might is explicitly a representation of supernatural power (i.e Charms), and the book actually says not to use BGs to represent Dragon-Blooded unless they gather in &quot;numbers&quot; almost never seen in the 2nd age.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the rules for Battlegroups would probably mention how mote pools and charms for supernatural beings work in the context of BGs, since things like ghosts or Fae are likely to be represented as BGs. However, it does not, because those kind of advantages are abstracted away into the Might rating","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:06:33-07:00","id":914806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caffeine Delusions</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914622#post914622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear, this is not a reference to Conservation of Ninjutsu?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it is, because the Battle Group rules are intended to simulate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:40:54-07:00","id":914821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914611#post914611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It should be worse than a super-awesome heroic individual. But a bunch of average dudes getting together as a battle group shouldn't be worse than a single average dude.</div> </div> </div> </div>An average person who still stands apart from a battle group is a trivial opponent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, say my Essence 5 PCs attack the local Realm satrapy guarded by a legion, and in the battle there's a unit of 10 young Dragonblood low-ranking officers. Now, it should be worse than the DB general, or his Dragonlords, or his 3 champions who may be low-ranking but are masters of combat, sure. But it shouldn't be worse than 1 young low-ranking DB officer.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bIt's probably going to be, since that's the priority in the rules for battle groups. Your ten Dragon Blooded should really be individuals, even if the gulf in power is sufficient to regard them as trivial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Similarly, a battle group of ninjas isn't going to be as good as a single ninja. But that's because the single ninja is a stand-out Ninja, not just a low-ranking apprentice ninja.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's fitting to the genre for the lone, standout novice warrior to play out with a bit more focus and nuance than the faceless horde of elites.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T07:59:28-07:00","id":914829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIt's probably going to be, since that's the priority in the rules for battle groups. Your ten Dragon Blooded should really be individuals, even if the gulf in power is sufficient to regard them as trivial. </div> </div> </div>No way am I running a fight between 15 Essence 1-2 DBs, 5 essence 3 DBs, and 1 essence 4 DB, vs 6 Essence 5 Solars. Especially when each side has several Size 5 Battlegroups of mortals as well. And demons.<br /> You can say &quot;oh, they should be individuals&quot;... but no. That's just not practical. Plus, they wouldn't be very good and would mostly provide initiative.<br /> It's much more practical to roll the 15 essence 1 DBs into a battle group, since that will actually be a very dangerous threat, if it's using charms. And 15 DBs ought to be a threat, even if they're only Essence 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Plus, this whole argument about DBs could be replaced with demons or elementals. I don't want PC sorcerers to feel that summoning more than 1 Blood Ape actually makes them worse at fighting.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T11:09:17-07:00","id":914927,"title":"","content":"Man I really need to get better at reading threads before I reply<br /> For what it's worth, unless every single one of those solars has significant combat investment I can't imagine that fight lasting very long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 06-15-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T12:23:56-07:00","id":914980,"title":"","content":"I would give a DB battle group excellencies, but not more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:36:09-07:00","id":915043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=914829#post914829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No way am I running a fight between 15 Essence 1-2 DBs, 5 essence 3 DBs, and 1 essence 4 DB, vs 6 Essence 5 Solars. Especially when each side has several Size 5 Battlegroups of mortals as well. And demons.<br /> You can say &quot;oh, they should be individuals&quot;... but no. That's just not practical. Plus, they wouldn't be very good and would mostly provide initiative.<br /> It's much more practical to roll the 15 essence 1 DBs into a battle group, since that will actually be a very dangerous threat, if it's using charms. And 15 DBs ought to be a threat, even if they're only Essence 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you should run smaller fights, where Exalted antagonists are concerned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Plus, this whole argument about DBs could be replaced with demons or elementals. I don't want PC sorcerers to feel that summoning more than 1 Blood Ape actually makes them worse at fighting.)</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a balance; one the one side, you get slightly higher dice pools, can be subject to the enhancement of command actions, and a modified way of taking damage that can be advantageous, but on the other you've got a character who can plausibly take a greater variety of actions, can have their Initiative adjusted, and can opt to make decisive attacks at any time.<br /> <br /> I think that last one is a major thing that can make individual characters situationally stronger than battle groups; they can elect to go straight for the health levels, either in circumstances of situational advantage, or when they're disadvantaged and don't really have much to lose; a battle group has to wear its targets down, which it can be slightly disadvantaged in against an enemy who can repeatedly replenish their Initiative off of the battle group attacking them.<br /> <br /> Battle groups are an abstraction for the sake of convenience and covering a measure of genre expectations; your sorcerer gets a bit of an advantage from using a group of demons as opposed to just one, but it's disproportionately to keep such groups from being overwhelmingly powerful, as they logically would be.<br /> <br /> In this case, though, it's mostly because battle groups is a system to represent mooks.<br /> <br /> Do you want your Dragon Blooded to be mooks?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:30:40-07:00","id":915082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915043#post915043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should run smaller fights, where Exalted antagonists are concerned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be pretty crappy to mess with the story just to avoid using mechanical abstractions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915043#post915043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a balance; one the one side, you get slightly higher dice pools, can be subject to the enhancement of command actions, and a modified way of taking damage that can be advantageous, but on the other you've got a character who can plausibly take a greater variety of actions, can have their Initiative adjusted, and can opt to make decisive attacks at any time.<br /> <br /> I think that last one is a major thing that can make individual characters situationally stronger than battle groups; they can elect to go straight for the health levels, either in circumstances of situational advantage, or when they're disadvantaged and don't really have much to lose; a battle group has to wear its targets down, which it can be slightly disadvantaged in against an enemy who can repeatedly replenish their Initiative off of the battle group attacking them.<br /> <br /> Battle groups are an abstraction for the sake of convenience and covering a measure of genre expectations; your sorcerer gets a bit of an advantage from using a group of demons as opposed to just one, but it's disproportionately to keep such groups from being overwhelmingly powerful, as they logically would be.<br /> <br /> In this case, though, it's mostly because battle groups is a system to represent mooks.<br /> <br /> Do you want your Dragon Blooded to be mooks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not letting the battle group use Charms makes them even mook-ier.<br /> <br /> And it creates insane situations where two blood apes is more than twice as dangerous as a dozen blood apes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:37:10-07:00","id":915088,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the examples I've seen of this sort of thing is abstracting the combat of the battlegroup. If you have 2 size 5 battlegroups fighting each other with their generals at the head, I think you can abstract most of those two Size 5 battlegroups fighting each other and just focus in on the Circle facing off against the other worthy opponents/maybe a smaller section of that battlegroup.<br /> <br /> The tricky part is that it can make the character commanding that battlegroup maybe feel undervalued because he can't command it, but the system seems intent on doing the Siege of Ostagar rather than a battle from Total War, y'know&gt;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:54:27-07:00","id":915107,"title":"","content":"We have an example of a DB buffing a BG by essentially granting his charms to it in the Antagonist section, for what its worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T14:55:48-07:00","id":915110,"title":"","content":"Personally, if there were multiple size 5 Battlegroups, I would shove them off into a narrative corner and not roll them out. I do think lumping low-essence DBs into a battlegroup when faced with five E5 Solars is valid, though. That starting Dynast is little better than a highly competent mortal when compared to a Night rolling in with twenty Archery charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:12:57-07:00","id":915120,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I'm not talking about whether or not a battle group uses Charms, I'm just assigning a higher value to the ability to make things like decisive attacks at will, change Initiative order, being a collection of separate health tracks that don't automatically create risks of the whole enemy force falling apart when you deplete the first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be pretty crappy to mess with the story just to avoid using mechanical abstractions.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI think systems are necessarily limited in how much they can be stretched, and that a scene in which there are more than about ten Exalted as a focus would be overbooked in a narrative sense even with a system that could effectively track them all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it creates insane situations where two blood apes is more than twice as dangerous as a dozen blood apes</div> </div> </div> </div> I think such situations are generally avoided by the fact that narrative justifications for those two blood apes to not be a miniscule battle group are few and far between, and on occasions in which such a justification exists then those two blood apes being so dangerous is entirely warranted.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way; are two player characters less dangerous than a battle group of four to six? As a battle group of up to fifty?<br /> <br /> Hell, battle groups do not even apply Onslaught penalties to Defense, which can be a major factor in making multiple individuals dangerous.<br /> <br /> I mean, doesn't the fact that a battle group models the assaults of up to several dozen people at a time as a single attack, that can only be withering imply that they're less dangerous than a small number of individuals who can make separate attacks all on its own?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T16:43:25-07:00","id":915181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915082#post915082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would be pretty crappy to mess with the story just to avoid using mechanical abstractions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not letting the battle group use Charms makes them even mook-ier.<br /> <br /> And it creates insane situations where two blood apes is more than twice as dangerous as a dozen blood apes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Any two combatants are stronger than a size 1 BG of those same combatants. That is just how battlegroups work, and why the book discourages you to use them to represent powerful beings like Dragon-Blooded. Its not so absurd if any amount of blood apes (or whatever) greater than 1 is represented as a battlegroup, so there is never a situation where two blood apes are stronger than a dozen. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11652-putty","name":"putty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T18:44:57-07:00","id":915253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, doesn't the fact that a battle group models the assaults of up to several dozen people at a time as a single attack, that can only be withering imply that they're less dangerous than a small number of individuals who can make separate attacks all on its own? </div> </div> </div>Yes? So why make them even worse?<br /> That's my main point. Battle groups are already a bit worse than 2-3 single people most of the time, for the (important) sake of ease of play. One of my PCs who plays a sorcerer was already (understandably) a little annoyed when I told him his 6 greenmaws were a size 1 battle group (because combats between 6 PCs and whoever are already complicated enough without throwing in 6 allies for the PCs), since of course it makes them weaker than if they were single creatures.<br /> I don't see a reason to nerf Battle Groups further by banning them from using charms.<br /> <br /> Now, you are right, I could simply not have the PCs fight so many DBs at once. But as Sanctaphrax points out, it seems lame to change the story for a mechanical abstraction. Ledaal Kes is a good enough strategist that he's going to know that feeding his 30-40 DBs to the Essence 5 PCs in groups of 5 at a time is just going to get them killed 5 at a time. The only chance he has to take down 2 Lunars and 2-4 Solars (it's not entirely clear how many Solars the PCs have) is to use all the resources he can, including junior DBs who by themselves would do little against a Dawn with Supernal Resistance and a Full Moon who turns into a 20-foot high super-elephant.<br /> <br /> It seems much easier for me to roll the junior DBs into a size 1 or 2, Might 2, high-stat battle group with excellencies (since they'd likely have a mix of charms and aspects, they probably don't have enough shared charms to use anything beyond excellencies). That'd actually be dangerous for the PCs, especially when being commanded by the Experienced DB QC and fighting alongside some Immaculate Monks.<br /> <br /> (And I probably would have the legions and their own troops fight in the background without rolls, but one of the PCs has like 20 War charms, so he might be trying to throw buffs onto his troops rather than stabbing Dragonblood)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-15-2016, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T19:11:26-07:00","id":915274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>putty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915181#post915181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any two combatants are stronger than a size 1 BG of those same combatants. That is just how battlegroups work, and why the book discourages you to use them to represent powerful beings like Dragon-Blooded. Its not so absurd if any amount of blood apes (or whatever) greater than 1 is represented as a battlegroup, so there is never a situation where two blood apes are stronger than a dozen.</div> </div> </div> </div>If two blood apes are, together, more dangerous than a Size 1 BG of blood apes...I can deal. If each of those two blood apes is more dangerous than the entire battle group, we have a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T01:31:25-07:00","id":915461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915253#post915253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ledaal Kes is a good enough strategist that he's going to know that feeding his 30-40 DBs to the Essence 5 PCs in groups of 5 at a time is just going to get them killed 5 at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting, because I've consistently found breaking up attackers to create multi-tiered encounters one of the more effective ways of challenging my PCs and obviously this scenario would need padding and context so it didn't seem like the early waves were kamikazes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T05:15:22-07:00","id":915524,"title":"","content":"Really? That's interesting. Is it because they're wounded and out of motes? Because I find that taking actual damage is rare, and of course them being crashed is something they've recovered from by the next combat. The only thing really is motes, and it's not generally a massive thing.<br /> <br /> I suppose I could send 5, then 5 20 minutes later (when they haven't recovered any motes), etc, but that'll take ages and ages to run.<br /> <br /> (In terms of early waves being kamikazes... how about sending bound demons in? Ones stupid enough to not know they are kamikazes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:01:32-07:00","id":915546,"title":"","content":"Mostly motes and willpower, actual damage is rare for me too but I value the ability to force the known heavy hitters to hold back.<br /> I don't view the gap between one scene and another as a 20 minute interval so much as a change of context I've devoted multiple sessions to a conflict that could in theory be resolved in one combat but realised that'd be a pain in the ass and/or extremely anti-climactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:27:42-07:00","id":915558,"title":"","content":"If it was me, I would want to present 40 Dragon Blooded at once as a fight that no Solar wants to have, ever. I would hope for a group that would take that at face value and thus engage in actions in their own right designed to advance the story of dividing this improbably large and focused group of Exalted up into manageable encounters. If the group was less cooperative, I would attempt to figure out some straightforward way of creating something that would approximate the danger of having 40 Dragon Blooded barrage you with attacks as individuals, to encourage them; that's the Orichalcum Rule in action, both in extending the rules to cover a possibility not really accounted for in the core of the game, and adjusting the rules to produce a result that makes sense to me.<br /> <br /> Even if you let them use individual Charms, I do not think a Size 2, Might 3 battle group sufficiently resembles the danger I would attribute to several dozen Dragon Blooded at once, especially when faced with a circle of Essence 5 Solars.<br /> <br /> If The Wizard of Oz has done so and felt it represented a sufficiently credible representation of fighting so many Exalted, then more power to him, but I think it is a matter where either our standards would be sufficiently different, or that it's not a result that could be relied upon consistently.<br /> <br /> All of this still based around a scenario that I think would be really, really unlikely to happen; thus, that the rules do not exactly extend to them is not a failure of the rules.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Alternatively, if I really needed to represent a few dozen Dragon Blooded at once as a battle group, then I'd try to run it on modified rules for how a battle group's Initiative and damage to Magnitude work, if only to avoid a representation that implies that very strike from a player character is Incapacitating three or four Exalted in one hit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-16-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:38:48-07:00","id":918081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/910996-3rd-edition-lookshy-and-solars?p=915274#post915274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If two blood apes are, together, more dangerous than a Size 1 BG of blood apes...I can deal. If each of those two blood apes is more dangerous than the entire battle group, we have a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You either want PC to deal with a horde of demons, because it is cool and thematic, but you do not really care about one on one combat with the demons, you make them BG and might them some special gambits to represent their powers. You might select one special snowflake Blood Ape trained personally by Octavian himself as their commander to show case him in one on one encounter. Different tools for different purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T09:59:44-07:00","id":918092,"title":"","content":"Lookshy response to Anathema depends on what story you want to tell. To bring it closer to home think about Catholics dealing with Devil/demons/heathens.<br /> <br /> In the &quot;ideal&quot; world all your believers are sincere and pure of faith, they have been warned about the honey tongued Devil and his deals, their response will be swift, decisive and not good for the Devil. Good example of faith like this would be the highly apocryphal <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Children%27s_Crusade\" target=\"_blank\">children crusades to free the holy lands</a>.<br /> <br /> A more pragmatic setting will probably result with a mix of true believers and cutthroat politicians, the later manipulating Anathema for their own purposes behind the back of the former.<br /> <br /> Then there is the real world &quot;example&quot; of freeing the holly lands, where among a lots of dead some people got very rich, made their grabs for power or just used the scene for power games.<br /> <br /> Read Dresden Files for an example of good people dealing with evil, because they just have no other better choice*, to fight bigger evil.<br /> * Disclaimer: There is always choice, the devil just makes sure to look it like there is none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}